1
00:00:00,484 --> 00:00:02,084
Since Myoung-Hwa joined...

2
00:00:02,285 --> 00:00:03,586
The team's energy changed.

3
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:04,728
Yes, completely!

4
00:00:04,729 --> 00:00:05,855
(Myoung-Hwa turned the game around.)

5
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:13,408
That was a good serve.

6
00:00:14,576 --> 00:00:16,010
Myoung-Hwa is rushing to defend!

7
00:00:16,011 --> 00:00:16,844
Myoung-Hwa!

8
00:00:17,879 --> 00:00:18,679
Go, Myoung-Hwa!

9
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,147
(Unbelievably fast diving dig)

10
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:23,050
Toss it up!

11
00:00:24,052 --> 00:00:25,119
Min Kyoung from Altos.

12
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,654
(Min Kyoung's push after a rally)

13
00:00:26,655 --> 00:00:27,622
Consecutive pushes.

14
00:00:27,622 --> 00:00:29,289
She blocked the ball and fell down.

15
00:00:31,626 --> 00:00:32,626
A push shot,

16
00:00:32,994 --> 00:00:34,094
and it worked!

17
00:00:34,095 --> 00:00:36,697
Chae-Rim scores with a clever soft tip!

18
00:00:36,698 --> 00:00:37,731
Don't rush, guys.

19
00:00:37,732 --> 00:00:39,466
(Slow down)

20
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:40,500
Don't rush it.

21
00:00:41,670 --> 00:00:43,270
They are in the lead now,

22
00:00:44,039 --> 00:00:46,507
- but they can't let their guards down.
- That's right.

23
00:00:47,809 --> 00:00:50,410
(Su Min's serve)

24
00:00:52,314 --> 00:00:53,714
It's a short one. It hit the net!

25
00:00:54,382 --> 00:00:56,416
Go for it! Run!

26
00:00:56,618 --> 00:00:58,118
They managed to save it.

27
00:00:58,119 --> 00:00:59,219
(Somehow saved it and sent it over)

28
00:01:01,022 --> 00:01:02,022
(Spike)

29
00:01:02,357 --> 00:01:04,491
Min Koung's spike hit the net,
and Wonder Dogs saved it!

30
00:01:04,492 --> 00:01:05,325
Na Yeon's ball.

31
00:01:05,327 --> 00:01:06,794
(Passing it to the left)

32
00:01:06,995 --> 00:01:07,861
Chae-Rim's spike!

33
00:01:08,396 --> 00:01:09,396
A diving dig.

34
00:01:10,098 --> 00:01:11,031
Back to Min Kyoung.

35
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:12,566
They blocked it.

36
00:01:13,501 --> 00:01:14,668
(The setter passed the ball too high.)

37
00:01:14,669 --> 00:01:15,602
(Barely sent it over)

38
00:01:16,438 --> 00:01:17,872
Seung Ju receives in defense.

39
00:01:17,872 --> 00:01:19,005
(Wonder Dogs' opportunity to score)

40
00:01:20,375 --> 00:01:21,408
(They're aiming for a comeback.)

41
00:01:21,409 --> 00:01:22,976
Wonder Dogs go for a counter!

42
00:01:24,079 --> 00:01:25,880
- Go for it!
- Go!

43
00:01:26,648 --> 00:01:28,849
(The ball goes off course in the air.)

44
00:01:29,451 --> 00:01:30,418
Na-Yeon!

45
00:01:33,555 --> 00:01:35,789
Yeon Jin sends the ball over,
but they block it.

46
00:01:37,492 --> 00:01:38,425
Min Kyoung.

47
00:01:41,796 --> 00:01:43,029
Come on, Na-Yeon!

48
00:01:43,031 --> 00:01:44,832
Sorry, I sent it too high. My bad.

49
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:47,067
(Na-Yeon's missed pass cost them a point.)

50
00:01:47,402 --> 00:01:48,869
Hey! Come on!

51
00:01:49,271 --> 00:01:50,204
Aren't you front row?

52
00:01:50,272 --> 00:01:51,138
I am.

53
00:01:52,774 --> 00:01:53,974
Where the heck are you passing to?

54
00:01:54,075 --> 00:01:54,941
Okay, coach.

55
00:01:56,111 --> 00:01:57,678
Just pass it in that direction!

56
00:01:57,679 --> 00:01:59,280
- Why here?
- Just pass it up!

57
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:06,020
Sorry.

58
00:02:06,154 --> 00:02:07,121
Just one point gap.

59
00:02:07,122 --> 00:02:10,658
(Second set, Altos 15 : Wonder Dogs 16)

60
00:02:11,192 --> 00:02:11,925
Go!

61
00:02:12,261 --> 00:02:13,093
- Go!
- Okay.

62
00:02:13,428 --> 00:02:14,028
Go!

63
00:02:15,130 --> 00:02:17,064
(Su Min's serve)

64
00:02:18,233 --> 00:02:19,066
A strong serve.

65
00:02:19,501 --> 00:02:20,301
Passed it nicely.

66
00:02:23,171 --> 00:02:24,138
It's out.

67
00:02:24,572 --> 00:02:26,606
- Yes!
- It's in!

68
00:02:26,608 --> 00:02:27,441
That was in?

69
00:02:27,442 --> 00:02:29,310
(The referee calls it in.)

70
00:02:30,845 --> 00:02:31,678
In?

71
00:02:33,048 --> 00:02:33,814
It was out.

72
00:02:34,683 --> 00:02:35,516
Let's check it.

73
00:02:35,517 --> 00:02:37,017
- He says it's out.
- Let's give it a shot.

74
00:02:37,018 --> 00:02:38,919
(Requesting a video challenge)

75
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:39,753
In or out.

76
00:02:41,089 --> 00:02:43,457
(Each coach can request
two video challenges per set.)

77
00:02:44,225 --> 00:02:49,162
A video challenge was requested
to check for in or out.

78
00:02:50,799 --> 00:02:52,800
(It dropped outside the line.)

79
00:02:54,235 --> 00:02:56,136
It was out. Okay.

80
00:02:56,805 --> 00:02:57,772
Yes, out!

81
00:02:57,772 --> 00:02:59,339
After the video review,

82
00:02:59,908 --> 00:03:01,876
the ball is out.

83
00:03:01,876 --> 00:03:03,076
(One point to Altos)

84
00:03:03,445 --> 00:03:04,912
(Second set, Altos 16 : Wonder Dogs 16)

85
00:03:04,913 --> 00:03:06,514
(Wonder Dogs gives up the tie.)

86
00:03:06,514 --> 00:03:07,581
Let's seize this opportunity.

87
00:03:09,050 --> 00:03:10,250
Yeon Jin's slide attack.

88
00:03:11,052 --> 00:03:12,019
She scored.

89
00:03:12,721 --> 00:03:14,355
Toss it up!

90
00:03:15,123 --> 00:03:17,224
A strong strike, but it's blocked.

91
00:03:17,993 --> 00:03:19,927
In the end, if you lose the momentum,

92
00:03:19,928 --> 00:03:21,896
- you start losing points in a row.
- That's right.

93
00:03:22,964 --> 00:03:25,699
(Second set, Altos 19 : Wonder Dogs 18)

94
00:03:26,101 --> 00:03:28,869
(They quickly allowed a turnaround.)

95
00:03:29,571 --> 00:03:30,770
Yeon Jin. Hey, Yeon Jin!

96
00:03:31,206 --> 00:03:33,307
Keep an eye on Seung Ju. In front of you.

97
00:03:37,812 --> 00:03:39,713
Na-Yeon, get the ball. Block it.

98
00:03:40,482 --> 00:03:42,216
(A shaky pass)

99
00:03:43,118 --> 00:03:45,319
Go, Na-Yeon. Pass the ball!

100
00:03:45,587 --> 00:03:47,688
Go, Na-Yeon. Pass the ball!

101
00:03:47,922 --> 00:03:48,688
No, Na-Yeon!
Go, Na-Yeon!

102
00:03:49,958 --> 00:03:50,858
No, Na-Yeon!

103
00:03:50,859 --> 00:03:53,194
(Na-Yeon's unforced error)

104
00:03:53,194 --> 00:03:53,927
Go, Na-Yeon!

105
00:03:54,129 --> 00:03:55,229
Come on, Ne-Yeon!

106
00:03:56,631 --> 00:03:58,265
That was a bit disappointing.

107
00:03:58,266 --> 00:03:59,233
(Points lost in a row)

108
00:03:59,234 --> 00:04:00,534
- Come on, stay focused!
- Okay.

109
00:04:00,802 --> 00:04:02,636
(Second set, Altos 20 : Wonder Dogs 18)

110
00:04:02,637 --> 00:04:03,470
Two-points gap.

111
00:04:03,905 --> 00:04:05,706
Nice defense, team Altos!

112
00:04:05,707 --> 00:04:06,941
(Second set, Altos 20 : Wonder Dogs 18)

113
00:04:06,941 --> 00:04:10,277
They say the setter is the mom
on the court,

114
00:04:10,346 --> 00:04:13,980
so if the setter loses her focus,
the others might lose their confidence.

115
00:04:13,982 --> 00:04:16,484
(A setter off her rhythm can
put the team at risk.)

116
00:04:16,518 --> 00:04:19,320
Yeon Jin, it's okay. Take your time.

117
00:04:20,155 --> 00:04:23,090
(Unlike Wonder Dogs,
Altos' energy is rising.)

118
00:04:23,958 --> 00:04:25,859
(They make a steady setup...)

119
00:04:27,362 --> 00:04:28,229
(followed by a strong finish.)

120
00:04:28,897 --> 00:04:30,365
- Nice pass.
- Nice work.

121
00:04:30,366 --> 00:04:31,832
Their offense pays off.

122
00:04:33,168 --> 00:04:35,436
(Another chance for Altos to score)

123
00:04:37,906 --> 00:04:40,074
(And they scored from a touch-out.)

124
00:04:40,842 --> 00:04:42,142
Nice pass.

125
00:04:42,644 --> 00:04:44,545
They're solid. That was a good hit.

126
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:45,912
Seize this momentum.

127
00:04:45,914 --> 00:04:47,381
It's 23 to 20 now.

128
00:04:47,382 --> 00:04:50,551
(Second set, Altos 23 : Wonder Dogs 20)

129
00:04:51,352 --> 00:04:53,586
(Coach Ho Chul calls for a substitution.)

130
00:04:53,588 --> 00:04:56,924
(Player in and player out)

131
00:04:58,493 --> 00:05:01,662
Ui Jeong comes in for Su Bin.

132
00:05:02,030 --> 00:05:04,131
Altos is bringing up their defense now,
along with the serve.

133
00:05:04,999 --> 00:05:06,766
She normally plays as a libero.

134
00:05:07,268 --> 00:05:08,134
Chae Yeon.

135
00:05:08,136 --> 00:05:10,537
(They're looking to cement their lead
by reinforcing their defense.)

136
00:05:11,573 --> 00:05:13,073
(Wonder Dogs have to turn
the game around.)

137
00:05:13,074 --> 00:05:15,409
Na-Yeon.
Look out for the low blocking here.

138
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:17,310
(They can’t afford to lose another point.)

139
00:05:17,312 --> 00:05:18,746
I thought we were doomed.

140
00:05:18,746 --> 00:05:21,881
We're always under pressure
that we cannot lose,

141
00:05:21,883 --> 00:05:23,550
so I was really nervous.

142
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:26,386
(Deep breath)

143
00:05:30,825 --> 00:05:31,825
Save it!

144
00:05:31,826 --> 00:05:34,194
(The pass went too far.)

145
00:05:34,796 --> 00:05:35,729
No!

146
00:05:36,698 --> 00:05:37,665
No!

147
00:05:37,665 --> 00:05:39,633
(Missed attack)

148
00:05:40,502 --> 00:05:41,769
Not a good pass.

149
00:05:41,769 --> 00:05:44,304
(Na-Yeon's pass error)

150
00:05:46,074 --> 00:05:47,374
Young In, I'm sorry.

151
00:05:48,411 --> 00:05:51,412
(A critical mistake at a crucial moment)

152
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:53,614
It's 24 to 20.

153
00:05:53,615 --> 00:05:55,649
This is Altos' second set point.

154
00:05:56,184 --> 00:05:59,520
- Let's go, Altos!
- Let's go, Altos!

155
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:01,454
(Only one point to victory for Altos.)

156
00:06:03,458 --> 00:06:07,861
(At this rate, Altos is going to win
the second set as well.)

157
00:06:08,997 --> 00:06:10,931
(This would be a crushing loss
for Wonder Dogs.)

158
00:06:11,933 --> 00:06:15,869
We made too many errors on our side.

159
00:06:17,071 --> 00:06:22,175
I kept thinking
about what I could do to help the team.

160
00:06:23,211 --> 00:06:25,813
Let's use ours. Let's use it.

161
00:06:27,115 --> 00:06:28,515
Net violation.

162
00:06:29,117 --> 00:06:31,218
She's requesting a video challenge.

163
00:06:31,219 --> 00:06:33,620
Why the heck would you pass like that?

164
00:06:34,722 --> 00:06:36,256
They didn't even push the ball over.

165
00:06:36,257 --> 00:06:37,791
I think she wanted a timeout.

166
00:06:37,792 --> 00:06:39,092
She just wanted a timeout.

167
00:06:39,327 --> 00:06:41,094
She just called it to get some time.

168
00:06:41,095 --> 00:06:42,062
They're out of timeouts.

169
00:06:42,463 --> 00:06:44,597
Wonder Dogs used up both their timeouts.

170
00:06:45,033 --> 00:06:48,803
Coach Kim could be
using this chance to get some time.

171
00:06:48,804 --> 00:06:52,640
And she probably meant to put a stop
to this momentum.

172
00:06:53,041 --> 00:06:55,175
- We're not passing to the left side.
- No, not to the left.

173
00:06:55,176 --> 00:06:58,145
- Remember, pass to the left side.
- Okay, coach.

174
00:06:58,646 --> 00:07:01,982
They have low blocking.
Just hit the ball there.

175
00:07:02,283 --> 00:07:03,483
Keep doing what you've been doing,

176
00:07:03,484 --> 00:07:04,285
but don't make mistakes.

177
00:07:04,286 --> 00:07:05,886
Just before, when Na-Yeon...

178
00:07:05,887 --> 00:07:08,088
got an easy ball,
she passed it on to Young In.

179
00:07:08,089 --> 00:07:09,556
Just don't make mistakes like that, okay?

180
00:07:10,358 --> 00:07:13,994
(He's still confident.)

181
00:07:13,995 --> 00:07:16,530
And remember, they do short serves.

182
00:07:16,531 --> 00:07:18,132
Check it first,
and then move on to the back.

183
00:07:18,132 --> 00:07:20,000
- Look out for the short serves first.
- Got it.

184
00:07:20,935 --> 00:07:23,470
- If you don't have it, just pass it.
- Okay.

185
00:07:23,471 --> 00:07:25,172
It's okay. Just relax.

186
00:07:25,173 --> 00:07:27,374
Hit it with confidence, Myoung-Hwa.
I'll cover you.

187
00:07:27,375 --> 00:07:28,175
Okay.

188
00:07:28,176 --> 00:07:30,477
(Using the break to reset the rhythm)

189
00:07:32,013 --> 00:07:33,914
(No wonder, it was not a net violation.)

190
00:07:34,549 --> 00:07:38,352
(Coach Ho Chul looks calm and confident.)

191
00:07:39,921 --> 00:07:42,022
(The crowd is fired up too.)

192
00:07:42,690 --> 00:07:44,557
Come on. Let's stay focused!

193
00:07:45,860 --> 00:07:48,562
I just want to win,
no matter what it takes.

194
00:07:48,896 --> 00:07:51,498
I don't even care
whether I do well in this game.

195
00:07:53,001 --> 00:07:53,801
We need to win this.

196
00:07:56,271 --> 00:07:57,171
Remember, to the left.
(It's not over...)

197
00:07:58,673 --> 00:08:01,408
(until it's over.)

198
00:08:02,377 --> 00:08:03,844
(Please...)

199
00:08:04,679 --> 00:08:07,347
(Su Bin's serve at a crucial moment)

200
00:08:10,885 --> 00:08:11,718
Go!

201
00:08:13,119 --> 00:08:15,233
(The ball is lifted to the left.)

202
00:08:15,809 --> 00:08:18,578
(Target position two,
where the blocking is low.)

203
00:08:20,247 --> 00:08:22,816
(As planned,
she set the ball to the left.)

204
00:08:22,817 --> 00:08:23,817
Chae-Rim!

205
00:08:25,965 --> 00:08:27,917
That was an accurate smash!

206
00:08:27,929 --> 00:08:29,503
Chae-Rim did a good job.

207
00:08:29,504 --> 00:08:33,193
(We still have hope.)

208
00:08:33,645 --> 00:08:34,645
Let's go!

209
00:08:36,029 --> 00:08:39,666
(They close the gap to three points.)

210
00:08:40,947 --> 00:08:42,268
Na-Yeon, you're doing great.

211
00:08:42,513 --> 00:08:44,571
- You just need your will.
- I went overboard.

212
00:08:44,673 --> 00:08:47,841
- Let's focus on defense!
- We've got this!

213
00:08:48,642 --> 00:08:51,311
(They're desperate for one point.)

214
00:08:52,894 --> 00:08:55,868
A lot is riding on Myoung-Hwa's serve.

215
00:08:55,869 --> 00:08:56,750
(The server is Myoung-Hwa.)

216
00:08:57,251 --> 00:08:59,587
(Will the ace server deliver again
this time?)

217
00:09:15,869 --> 00:09:19,272
(Her serve shook them once again!)

218
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:21,382
(Closing the gap in an instant,
by one point.)

219
00:09:21,909 --> 00:09:24,044
(Well done, Myoung-Hwa.)

220
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,707
I love Myoung-Hwa so much.

221
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:28,486
She's the true ace of set two.

222
00:09:29,794 --> 00:09:32,353
You! Chae Won!

223
00:09:32,761 --> 00:09:35,801
Chae Won should move out wide,
and you should step in!

224
00:09:35,802 --> 00:09:37,424
Why are both of you standing
for the serve receive?

225
00:09:39,359 --> 00:09:41,928
(The Altos are starting
to show some cracks.)

226
00:09:42,684 --> 00:09:44,965
Na Hee.

227
00:09:47,067 --> 00:09:49,036
Focus on the position.

228
00:09:49,503 --> 00:09:52,973
(The target of both attack and blocking
is position two.)

229
00:09:54,029 --> 00:09:56,577
It's forward!

230
00:09:57,448 --> 00:09:58,715
Quick attack.

231
00:09:59,313 --> 00:10:00,618
(Leaking the wrong plan)

232
00:10:00,619 --> 00:10:02,292
Quick attack!

233
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:05,719
The score is 24 to 22.

234
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:09,696
For Myoung-Hwa's performance to shine,
they must take this set.

235
00:10:09,890 --> 00:10:11,525
- Nice serve!
- Nice serve!

236
00:10:11,558 --> 00:10:12,826
(Screaming)

237
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:18,298
(They're shaken again.)

238
00:10:22,102 --> 00:10:24,471
(Moving to the assigned position)

239
00:10:25,038 --> 00:10:27,173
(Na Hee, you know what I'm saying, right?)

240
00:10:30,077 --> 00:10:32,467
(Of course, I do.)

241
00:10:32,468 --> 00:10:34,867
The Wonder Dogs' blocking worked!

242
00:10:35,048 --> 00:10:38,084
(The volleyball legend's strategy
worked perfectly.)

243
00:10:41,082 --> 00:10:43,275
- Yes!
- Yes!

244
00:10:44,591 --> 00:10:45,601
Let's go!

245
00:10:46,627 --> 00:10:48,685
(The momentum is on our side.)

246
00:10:48,704 --> 00:10:51,231
It's all thanks
to Myoung-Hwa's great serve.

247
00:10:54,203 --> 00:10:55,330
There were other options...

248
00:10:56,203 --> 00:10:58,172
(Trying to be patient)

249
00:10:59,973 --> 00:11:02,275
(It all comes down to a single point.)

250
00:11:03,410 --> 00:11:06,013
(The Altos players are very tense.)

251
00:11:07,494 --> 00:11:09,583
Let's just score one more point.
Focus on defense.

252
00:11:09,941 --> 00:11:12,628
Don't do this, Na-Yeon.

253
00:11:14,955 --> 00:11:16,177
The same strategy.

254
00:11:16,178 --> 00:11:17,178
Position two?

255
00:11:19,459 --> 00:11:22,062
(The serve ace herself is a threat.)

256
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,143
The reception is shaking.

257
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:32,405
(The block at the second position
is broken.)

258
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:34,375
(Calm down!)

259
00:11:35,075 --> 00:11:36,677
(Where's the ball going?)

260
00:11:37,171 --> 00:11:38,498
That was a confident move.

261
00:11:38,499 --> 00:11:39,713
(Nice catch by Na-Yeon)

262
00:11:40,247 --> 00:11:40,948
That's it.

263
00:11:42,488 --> 00:11:43,817
(The second touch goes to Myoung-Hwa.)

264
00:11:45,652 --> 00:11:46,753
(Attack failed.)

265
00:11:47,888 --> 00:11:49,757
(The only remaining attacker is Young In.)

266
00:11:49,999 --> 00:11:51,754
(They need to finish this
with a powerful hit.)

267
00:11:51,779 --> 00:11:53,259
Young In tips over the net.

268
00:11:54,246 --> 00:11:55,246
Young In!

269
00:11:57,397 --> 00:11:59,432
(The ball goes
to the opponent's court helplessly.)

270
00:12:03,804 --> 00:12:05,539
(The ball is saved.)

271
00:12:07,741 --> 00:12:08,208
(Fast)

272
00:12:09,009 --> 00:12:09,977
(Swift)

273
00:12:13,663 --> 00:12:17,133
(Myoung-Hwa is running.)

274
00:12:17,562 --> 00:12:19,735
- Myoung-Hwa!
- Myoung-Hwa saved it!

275
00:12:20,594 --> 00:12:21,995
- Myoung-Hwa!
- Myoung-Hwa saved it!

276
00:12:23,390 --> 00:12:25,392
(Escaping the crisis with a super dig)

277
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,208
Hit it, Young In!

278
00:12:28,762 --> 00:12:29,997
(Altos' chance ball)

279
00:12:31,364 --> 00:12:32,532
(Min Kyoung is ready to attack.)

280
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,169
(We must block.)

281
00:12:35,669 --> 00:12:38,372
(We must get through.)

282
00:12:42,270 --> 00:12:45,445
- They didn't touch it.
- The spike hit the net!

283
00:12:45,725 --> 00:12:47,983
This is unbelievable!

284
00:12:48,181 --> 00:12:49,983
(Screaming)

285
00:12:50,517 --> 00:12:52,686
(At a loss for words)

286
00:12:53,560 --> 00:12:56,656
(The Altos' huge mistake)

287
00:12:59,758 --> 00:13:01,862
The Wonder Dogs have a chance
to turn things around.

288
00:13:01,863 --> 00:13:03,997
(Finally, it's tied.)

289
00:13:07,247 --> 00:13:10,774
Sure. Everyone knows Myoung-Hwa is good
at blocking and serving.

290
00:13:10,987 --> 00:13:13,634
But how could she even be good at defense?

291
00:13:13,853 --> 00:13:16,165
She's never shown such a performance
in the pro league.

292
00:13:17,177 --> 00:13:19,146
(Can you believe it's tied?)

293
00:13:19,179 --> 00:13:21,181
(Jumping around)

294
00:13:21,499 --> 00:13:22,749
This is crazy.

295
00:13:24,484 --> 00:13:26,853
(The warmup zone is
also erupting with cheers.)

296
00:13:29,790 --> 00:13:32,359
(While the spectators are
cheering with joy...)

297
00:13:35,374 --> 00:13:36,830
Why did you do the feint there?

298
00:13:38,098 --> 00:13:42,235
(Pointing out Young In's passive play)

299
00:13:43,436 --> 00:13:45,338
(Oh, gosh.)

300
00:13:45,772 --> 00:13:50,043
(The play matters
more than the point right now.)

301
00:13:51,211 --> 00:13:52,211
You're doing well.

302
00:13:53,098 --> 00:13:54,098
Young In.

303
00:13:56,617 --> 00:13:58,004
- How was the ball?
- Good.

304
00:13:58,005 --> 00:14:01,021
It's okay. Just hit it.
You're an opposite hitter.

305
00:14:01,022 --> 00:14:02,529
Try it again.

306
00:14:03,456 --> 00:14:04,643
(Altos 24 : Wonder Dogs 20)

307
00:14:04,644 --> 00:14:07,961
(Altos 24 : Wonder Dogs 22)

308
00:14:07,962 --> 00:14:09,429
(Altos 24 : Wonder Dogs 23)

309
00:14:09,430 --> 00:14:11,230
(Altos 24 : Wonder Dogs 24)

310
00:14:12,132 --> 00:14:14,167
(The Wonder Dogs have
caught up four points.)

311
00:14:14,842 --> 00:14:17,637
(Deuce: It happens when the score is
tied with just one point left to win.)

312
00:14:17,637 --> 00:14:20,039
(The side that scores
two consecutive points wins.)

313
00:14:20,373 --> 00:14:24,110
(They're back to square one!)

314
00:14:24,578 --> 00:14:30,284
(Either we end it, or they do!)

315
00:14:30,867 --> 00:14:33,520
Na Hee, the same plan!

316
00:14:35,135 --> 00:14:37,841
(Leaking the fake play again)

317
00:14:38,258 --> 00:14:40,227
(Let's go, the ace server!)

318
00:14:48,953 --> 00:14:50,170
Toss it again!

319
00:14:52,505 --> 00:14:53,228
Here!

320
00:14:53,229 --> 00:14:54,229
Min Kyoung!

321
00:14:54,230 --> 00:14:55,008
(Flinch)

322
00:14:55,221 --> 00:14:56,543
It landed inside the line.

323
00:14:57,177 --> 00:15:00,814
(They scored first
with Min Kyoung's outstanding play.)

324
00:15:02,975 --> 00:15:04,718
Myoung-Hwa!

325
00:15:04,787 --> 00:15:07,721
They've brought it to a deuce
with Myoung-Hwa's great serve.

326
00:15:07,722 --> 00:15:09,322
I told you not to step in.

327
00:15:10,083 --> 00:15:13,903
- Yeon Jin, you did well. Relax!
- Okay!

328
00:15:13,929 --> 00:15:15,269
Na-Yeon, what should you do here?

329
00:15:16,263 --> 00:15:21,068
(This rookie coach also checks
the tactical plan until the end.)

330
00:15:21,508 --> 00:15:24,171
(If they concede one point here,)

331
00:15:24,537 --> 00:15:27,240
(Set Two is over.)

332
00:15:33,113 --> 00:15:34,481
(Barely digging the ball)

333
00:15:35,472 --> 00:15:37,119
- There's no one!
- There's no one!

334
00:15:37,957 --> 00:15:39,215
There's no attacker in position.

335
00:15:39,749 --> 00:15:40,749
Where are you setting it?

336
00:15:41,365 --> 00:15:43,456
It's a chance.

337
00:15:44,869 --> 00:15:45,869
Na-Yeon.

338
00:15:45,870 --> 00:15:47,160
(A toss to the left)

339
00:15:47,961 --> 00:15:51,465
(The ball is set as planned.)

340
00:15:56,836 --> 00:15:58,404
(Chae-Rim's powerful hit)

341
00:15:59,928 --> 00:16:01,942
- It's Chae-Rim again!
- Chae-Rim!

342
00:16:01,943 --> 00:16:03,943
- Nice play!
- They catch up again!

343
00:16:04,311 --> 00:16:07,381
(It's a tie again!)

344
00:16:07,681 --> 00:16:09,850
(Shouting)

345
00:16:11,026 --> 00:16:12,026
Hey...

346
00:16:15,322 --> 00:16:17,491
(Blinking)

347
00:16:17,565 --> 00:16:18,565
A deuce again!

348
00:16:18,566 --> 00:16:21,531
(Feeling dizzy
at the Wonder Dogs' powerful hit)

349
00:16:21,550 --> 00:16:22,550
Good job.

350
00:16:22,551 --> 00:16:26,599
(They're on a roll.)

351
00:16:29,643 --> 00:16:31,505
Chae-Rim, nice play!

352
00:16:32,372 --> 00:16:33,473
(My throat soars.)

353
00:16:33,642 --> 00:16:35,305
Na-Yeon!

354
00:16:35,306 --> 00:16:37,577
Good job.

355
00:16:39,879 --> 00:16:43,449
(The score is back to even.)

356
00:16:44,250 --> 00:16:46,085
(A sign for a targeted serve)

357
00:16:51,622 --> 00:16:52,622
(Screaming)

358
00:16:59,431 --> 00:17:01,868
(Will the serve catch the net?)

359
00:17:02,402 --> 00:17:05,005
(Will it be a point loss on serve?)

360
00:17:10,310 --> 00:17:12,096
Serve ace!

361
00:17:12,136 --> 00:17:14,589
She scored a serve ace
and turned the game around!

362
00:17:16,249 --> 00:17:19,986
(The table is turned around.)

363
00:17:21,087 --> 00:17:25,024
(The ace server is super satisfied.)

364
00:17:25,328 --> 00:17:27,468
Yes! Young In!

365
00:17:27,781 --> 00:17:31,820
Catching up from that score is never easy.

366
00:17:31,832 --> 00:17:33,666
The game isn't over
as long as you don't give up.

367
00:17:34,834 --> 00:17:37,870
(Already three serve aces in Set Two)

368
00:17:38,304 --> 00:17:42,141
(Pooh)

369
00:17:42,841 --> 00:17:45,164
It's all right. Let's do this.

370
00:17:45,165 --> 00:17:47,746
(In an instant, joy and despair split.)

371
00:17:48,248 --> 00:17:51,118
(They're freezing up.)

372
00:17:53,616 --> 00:17:55,722
Slow down!

373
00:17:57,419 --> 00:17:58,619
Young In!

374
00:17:58,620 --> 00:18:00,292
(Busy reminding the players
of the set plans)

375
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:02,395
This is our plan.

376
00:18:02,838 --> 00:18:05,382
Chae-Rim, look. This is our plan.

377
00:18:05,466 --> 00:18:08,289
With a score of 26 to 25,
it's the Wonder Dogs have set point!

378
00:18:09,501 --> 00:18:13,305
(Victory is within reach!)

379
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:16,393
Nice!

380
00:18:16,645 --> 00:18:18,345
(Their reception is shaky!)

381
00:18:18,345 --> 00:18:19,978
The reception is unstable.

382
00:18:21,411 --> 00:18:23,545
(Hwang Min Kyoung's spike)

383
00:18:24,878 --> 00:18:26,778
It didn't touch the hands!

384
00:18:27,978 --> 00:18:29,978
It didn't touch the hands!

385
00:18:30,011 --> 00:18:31,245
The ball didn't hit them!

386
00:18:31,878 --> 00:18:33,778
Wasn't that a four-hit?

387
00:18:35,244 --> 00:18:38,811
(But the game continues,)

388
00:18:41,244 --> 00:18:43,211
(and the point stands for the Altos.)

389
00:18:43,644 --> 00:18:45,178
It didn't hit the hands!

390
00:18:45,178 --> 00:18:47,111
(Wonder Dogs strongly claim
it's a four-hit.)

391
00:18:47,878 --> 00:18:49,278
(They request a video review.)

392
00:18:49,278 --> 00:18:52,078
(Why?)

393
00:18:53,078 --> 00:18:55,611
(The referee doesn't allow.)

394
00:18:55,744 --> 00:18:56,811
No, you can't!

395
00:18:57,344 --> 00:18:58,378
You can't.

396
00:18:59,511 --> 00:19:00,544
Not anymore.

397
00:19:01,011 --> 00:19:02,911
Will there be no video review?

398
00:19:02,911 --> 00:19:04,778
(They can't do a video review anymore?)

399
00:19:05,078 --> 00:19:08,811
(Early in the second set, they requested
a video review for a block touch.)

400
00:19:08,978 --> 00:19:11,011
(But it was called no touch.)

401
00:19:11,211 --> 00:19:13,044
(They used one video review.)

402
00:19:13,211 --> 00:19:14,744
(And just now,)

403
00:19:14,744 --> 00:19:16,978
(they asked for a video review
instead of a timeout.)

404
00:19:16,978 --> 00:19:19,311
(All their opportunities are used.)

405
00:19:19,611 --> 00:19:20,711
You can't.

406
00:19:20,844 --> 00:19:23,044
(Because they can't do a video review,)

407
00:19:23,578 --> 00:19:24,744
(the point goes to the Altos.)

408
00:19:24,744 --> 00:19:25,911
They said, "No."

409
00:19:27,611 --> 00:19:31,144
Wonder Dogs stated
the ball didn't hit their hands.

410
00:19:31,144 --> 00:19:32,644
However...

411
00:19:36,011 --> 00:19:37,411
It's okay!

412
00:19:38,211 --> 00:19:40,211
- Na-Yeon, get ready to attack.
- The serve is short.

413
00:19:40,211 --> 00:19:41,811
(Second set, Altos 26: Wonder Dogs 26)

414
00:19:41,978 --> 00:19:43,078
Coach, do we bring them in?

415
00:19:43,611 --> 00:19:44,944
Get the two in!

416
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:49,444
(Are they using substitutions
to end the game?)

417
00:19:52,011 --> 00:19:54,678
Coach Kim Ho Chul brought
Kim Ha Kyung and Lee So Young in.

418
00:19:54,678 --> 00:19:56,378
It shows they're desperate.

419
00:19:56,378 --> 00:19:58,378
(Lee So Young and Kim Ha Kyung,
aces of their team, are in.)

420
00:20:03,611 --> 00:20:04,778
It's okay!

421
00:20:06,344 --> 00:20:08,444
I'm sure we can win.

422
00:20:10,378 --> 00:20:11,411
It's fine.

423
00:20:16,611 --> 00:20:17,611
Serve!

424
00:20:18,311 --> 00:20:19,344
The line!

425
00:20:21,278 --> 00:20:22,278
The line!

426
00:20:22,278 --> 00:20:24,411
(Wonder Dogs get a point.)

427
00:20:27,911 --> 00:20:30,344
She stepped on a service line!

428
00:20:30,344 --> 00:20:32,278
I saw it!

429
00:20:32,278 --> 00:20:33,344
Great job.

430
00:20:33,344 --> 00:20:34,744
(Ho Geun, the Hawkeye)

431
00:20:41,778 --> 00:20:44,211
She clearly stepped on the line.

432
00:20:44,211 --> 00:20:47,078
It's actually rare
to make errors like this.

433
00:20:47,844 --> 00:20:48,878
The line!

434
00:20:48,878 --> 00:20:53,011
(They score right away
thanks to an obvious error.)

435
00:20:57,444 --> 00:20:58,911
Ha Kyung stepped on the line.

436
00:21:01,444 --> 00:21:02,611
What the...

437
00:21:03,511 --> 00:21:06,644
(Trying to be patient again)

438
00:21:08,611 --> 00:21:12,211
Even a professional player
can make such mistakes.

439
00:21:12,211 --> 00:21:13,978
- Yeah. I saw that.
- It's okay!

440
00:21:14,144 --> 00:21:15,411
(Altos 26: Wonder Dogs 27)

441
00:21:15,411 --> 00:21:16,978
It's Wonder Dogs' set point again.

442
00:21:17,344 --> 00:21:18,378
Seung Ju!

443
00:21:21,911 --> 00:21:24,144
(Block first and then move.)

444
00:21:24,578 --> 00:21:26,444
(Understood.)

445
00:21:28,411 --> 00:21:30,911
(Just a point left before their win)

446
00:21:30,911 --> 00:21:33,244
(This single point...)

447
00:21:33,244 --> 00:21:35,211
(will decide the result of the set.)

448
00:21:35,211 --> 00:21:36,278
Catch!

449
00:21:36,278 --> 00:21:38,344
(Instructing endlessly)

450
00:21:38,744 --> 00:21:40,644
(Back Chae-Rim serves.)

451
00:21:43,378 --> 00:21:44,378
Lee So Young.

452
00:21:44,378 --> 00:21:46,078
(The Altos set up smoothly.)

453
00:21:47,078 --> 00:21:48,478
(Lee So Young's tip)

454
00:21:49,711 --> 00:21:50,711
A tip!

455
00:21:51,978 --> 00:21:53,844
(Nice cover)

456
00:21:54,744 --> 00:21:56,378
They must remain calm!

457
00:21:56,378 --> 00:21:57,644
(This is our chance.)

458
00:21:58,344 --> 00:22:00,178
(And Seung Ju is the hitter.)

459
00:22:00,378 --> 00:22:01,944
That's it!

460
00:22:02,311 --> 00:22:03,644
That's it!

461
00:22:04,378 --> 00:22:05,811
You already know about low blocks.

462
00:22:06,778 --> 00:22:08,678
Set the ball without mercy!

463
00:22:18,278 --> 00:22:20,011
They must remain calm!

464
00:22:20,011 --> 00:22:21,044
Spike!

465
00:22:21,044 --> 00:22:22,944
(A successful hit)

466
00:22:22,944 --> 00:22:25,078
They won the second set!

467
00:22:25,244 --> 00:22:26,944
(Shouting and laughing)

468
00:22:26,944 --> 00:22:29,178
They won the second set!

469
00:22:30,344 --> 00:22:33,111
(The captain's decisive attack)

470
00:22:33,911 --> 00:22:36,844
(We won!)

471
00:22:37,378 --> 00:22:40,311
(Thrilling)

472
00:22:41,111 --> 00:22:44,844
(The underdogs' fierce counterattack)

473
00:22:49,311 --> 00:22:51,011
Way to go!

474
00:22:51,944 --> 00:22:54,844
There's Pyo Seung Ju's final spike.

475
00:22:54,844 --> 00:22:56,644
(Her attack breaks through the block.)

476
00:22:56,644 --> 00:22:59,611
I still can't believe what I just saw.

477
00:23:01,978 --> 00:23:04,944
(Am I dreaming?)

478
00:23:06,378 --> 00:23:09,011
(The match is all square again!)

479
00:23:09,011 --> 00:23:11,211
What was the score before?

480
00:23:11,211 --> 00:23:12,478
Was it 20 to 24?

481
00:23:13,044 --> 00:23:14,078
- I don't know!
- You don't?

482
00:23:14,778 --> 00:23:16,678
- Nice!
- What a relief.

483
00:23:16,678 --> 00:23:18,778
(They confidently take a timeout
for the third set.)

484
00:23:18,778 --> 00:23:20,411
(You're the best!)

485
00:23:20,411 --> 00:23:22,378
(Families unite.)

486
00:23:22,778 --> 00:23:24,444
You did it, Na-Yeon!

487
00:23:24,678 --> 00:23:27,544
Sit down.

488
00:23:27,578 --> 00:23:29,011
Take a seat.

489
00:23:29,011 --> 00:23:30,211
It's okay, Young In. Sit down.

490
00:23:31,678 --> 00:23:33,544
(The rookie head coach reviews
the strategy.)

491
00:23:33,544 --> 00:23:34,544
Look.

492
00:23:35,244 --> 00:23:36,878
We have a higher success rate in attacks.

493
00:23:36,878 --> 00:23:37,944
That's great news.

494
00:23:38,344 --> 00:23:39,544
We might win.

495
00:23:39,544 --> 00:23:41,478
- We must beat them.
- You've got this.

496
00:23:41,478 --> 00:23:42,978
- What?
- We must win.

497
00:23:42,978 --> 00:23:46,578
(The third set will be the turning point.)

498
00:23:47,011 --> 00:23:50,078
(What's the new coach's plan?)

499
00:23:50,378 --> 00:23:51,578
Young In, come here.

500
00:23:53,044 --> 00:23:55,978
Try to hit the ball above Min Kyoung,
not to her sides.

501
00:23:55,978 --> 00:23:57,144
- Yes, Coach.
- Raise your arms.

502
00:23:57,144 --> 00:23:59,311
Here. Aim straight above Min Kyoung.

503
00:23:59,311 --> 00:24:00,378
Yes.

504
00:24:00,878 --> 00:24:03,011
(In the second set,)

505
00:24:03,944 --> 00:24:08,344
(targeting the left area
with low blocks worked well.)

506
00:24:09,544 --> 00:24:14,711
(However, they didn't use
the right side areas much.)

507
00:24:14,878 --> 00:24:17,311
If the team only attacks the left area,

508
00:24:17,311 --> 00:24:20,011
their opponents will mark that spot.

509
00:24:20,011 --> 00:24:21,378
And the attacks will get repetitive.

510
00:24:21,644 --> 00:24:23,644
You're not attacking
the right side at all.

511
00:24:23,644 --> 00:24:25,744
The rest are fine, including the tip.

512
00:24:25,744 --> 00:24:27,611
But you keep missing chances to attack.

513
00:24:27,611 --> 00:24:28,678
Yes, Coach.

514
00:24:28,678 --> 00:24:32,078
(First, when there are two blockers
on the other side,)

515
00:24:33,178 --> 00:24:36,478
(the team will hit the ball
over their reach to score.)

516
00:24:36,611 --> 00:24:38,344
But how should you attack
if you're too fast?

517
00:24:38,344 --> 00:24:39,911
- Go in between.
- Understood.

518
00:24:39,911 --> 00:24:42,111
Got it? In between and to that corner.

519
00:24:42,578 --> 00:24:45,511
(If the setter tosses quickly...)

520
00:24:46,211 --> 00:24:49,211
(and the middle blocker
of the opposing team comes late,)

521
00:24:49,644 --> 00:24:53,344
(they will hit the ball
in between the blocks to score.)

522
00:24:53,511 --> 00:24:55,111
Check their reception rate.

523
00:24:55,111 --> 00:24:56,478
- It's 59 percent.
- Yes.

524
00:24:56,478 --> 00:24:57,478
A 59 percent.

525
00:24:57,478 --> 00:24:59,311
Ui Jeong only has 29 percent.

526
00:24:59,311 --> 00:25:00,711
(Go Ui Jeong has a low reception rate.)

527
00:25:00,711 --> 00:25:02,411
- Aim for Go Ui Jeong.
- Yes, Coach.

528
00:25:04,011 --> 00:25:08,244
(Meanwhile, the Altos)

529
00:25:10,444 --> 00:25:11,578
Stick to the lineup.

530
00:25:14,278 --> 00:25:16,544
Go ahead. Just lose.

531
00:25:17,211 --> 00:25:19,111
Yeon Jin will stay,
and you'll all keep your positions.

532
00:25:24,344 --> 00:25:26,178
Do it properly when you're in.

533
00:25:26,178 --> 00:25:27,211
Yes!

534
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:32,278
- What are you doing in the middle?
- I'm sorry.

535
00:25:33,311 --> 00:25:35,144
Pull yourself together!

536
00:25:35,144 --> 00:25:36,344
Yes, Coach.

537
00:25:36,344 --> 00:25:37,978
I couldn't see you, Ui Jeong.

538
00:25:38,411 --> 00:25:39,878
I couldn't see you on the court.

539
00:25:41,044 --> 00:25:42,911
- Do you know what that means?
- I do.

540
00:25:43,878 --> 00:25:45,744
You're not doing anything.

541
00:25:45,744 --> 00:25:47,411
- Nothing at all.
- Understood.

542
00:25:53,678 --> 00:25:55,611
We're not here to mess around, are we?

543
00:25:56,878 --> 00:26:00,078
If we make ridiculous errors,
we'll lose our momentum.

544
00:26:00,078 --> 00:26:01,244
(Hwang Min Kyoung, the captain)

545
00:26:01,244 --> 00:26:02,444
Concentrate.

546
00:26:02,444 --> 00:26:04,111
We won't win if we go easy.

547
00:26:04,111 --> 00:26:05,244
Yes.

548
00:26:05,244 --> 00:26:06,278
Hey.

549
00:26:06,944 --> 00:26:09,011
Hey, one more thing.

550
00:26:09,178 --> 00:26:12,478
You're not supposed to be tied
at 24 points.

551
00:26:14,111 --> 00:26:15,478
What did you do?

552
00:26:15,478 --> 00:26:17,444
What have you done
when the score was 20 to 24?

553
00:26:17,778 --> 00:26:19,078
It's all our mistakes, isn't it?

554
00:26:19,078 --> 00:26:20,411
We made errors to lose points.

555
00:26:23,611 --> 00:26:24,811
Do you guys remember?

556
00:26:25,311 --> 00:26:26,378
Do you?

557
00:26:26,378 --> 00:26:27,978
You remember how you attacked?

558
00:26:28,144 --> 00:26:29,644
Yes, I do.

559
00:26:29,911 --> 00:26:31,444
- Don't do that next time.
- Okay.

560
00:26:31,444 --> 00:26:32,511
Focus.

561
00:26:34,144 --> 00:26:35,344
Let's do it again.

562
00:26:35,344 --> 00:26:37,478
Do it properly this time.

563
00:26:37,478 --> 00:26:38,578
Concentrate.

564
00:26:40,744 --> 00:26:42,311
Before the crucial third set,

565
00:26:42,311 --> 00:26:44,411
Hwang Min Kyoung is leading the team...

566
00:26:44,411 --> 00:26:46,244
- as their captain.
- Let's go.

567
00:26:46,544 --> 00:26:48,944
Go Ui Jeong's hits are strong as well.

568
00:26:48,944 --> 00:26:51,711
So Wonder Dogs should stay alert.

569
00:26:52,044 --> 00:26:54,578
They must maintain their momentum...

570
00:26:54,578 --> 00:26:56,644
and start strong in the third set.

571
00:26:57,644 --> 00:27:01,278
(Third set, Altos 0: Wonder Dogs 0)

572
00:27:01,444 --> 00:27:03,278
In 1, 2, 3. Nice serve!

573
00:27:03,278 --> 00:27:05,630
(Wonder Dogs' first serve by Na-Yeon)

574
00:27:06,098 --> 00:27:07,098
The third set begins.

575
00:27:09,599 --> 00:27:11,935
(A targeted serve aimed at Go Ui Jeong)

576
00:27:12,969 --> 00:27:15,138
(The opponent's reception destabilizes.)

577
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:20,343
- It's out.
- They score a point.

578
00:27:20,344 --> 00:27:21,544
Let's go!

579
00:27:21,952 --> 00:27:22,952
Young In.

580
00:27:23,758 --> 00:27:25,251
Young In, good job.

581
00:27:27,278 --> 00:27:30,320
- Now, the players seem more comfortable.
- That's right.

582
00:27:30,334 --> 00:27:34,657
Coach Kim seems to be focusing more
on the blocking line.

583
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:39,763
(A strong start with the first point)

584
00:27:40,563 --> 00:27:43,232
(Another serve by Na-Yeon)

585
00:27:43,233 --> 00:27:44,867
It's another serve by Na-Yeon.

586
00:27:45,771 --> 00:27:46,771
(Groaning)

587
00:27:49,639 --> 00:27:52,709
- It's out.
- A serve error.

588
00:27:55,347 --> 00:27:56,702
Na-Yeon, where are you aiming at?

589
00:27:57,153 --> 00:28:00,660
Na-Yeon, where are you aiming at?
Ui Jeong is right there! Think straight!

590
00:28:03,453 --> 00:28:06,589
(Your serve error is our pleasure!)

591
00:28:06,879 --> 00:28:08,491
Focus!

592
00:28:10,225 --> 00:28:11,225
The score is 1 to 1.

593
00:28:11,226 --> 00:28:13,429
(The score is back to square one.)

594
00:28:14,036 --> 00:28:16,966
(Ui Jeong's serve)

595
00:28:22,772 --> 00:28:24,774
(Setting to the right as planned)

596
00:28:25,908 --> 00:28:27,810
(Blocked?)

597
00:28:28,978 --> 00:28:32,181
(A spike through the gap,
not a straight shot)

598
00:28:36,917 --> 00:28:38,144
- Guys, go!
- The defender gets it.

599
00:28:38,697 --> 00:28:39,697
It was a bit low.

600
00:28:40,996 --> 00:28:42,358
- Hey!
- She receives and passes.

601
00:28:43,962 --> 00:28:45,912
Jump toss, and a setter dump!

602
00:28:45,913 --> 00:28:47,038
(The attack is blocked on the left too.)

603
00:28:47,039 --> 00:28:48,065
Myoung-Hwa saves it.

604
00:28:48,918 --> 00:28:49,918
That's it.

605
00:28:50,784 --> 00:28:51,784
It's a touch out.

606
00:28:51,785 --> 00:28:54,270
(Altos scores a point by a touch out.)

607
00:28:54,426 --> 00:28:56,829
Young In! Didn't you see who was there?

608
00:28:57,092 --> 00:28:59,732
Min Kyoung was right there!
You should've aimed at her!

609
00:29:02,145 --> 00:29:04,681
(Got it.)

610
00:29:05,038 --> 00:29:07,583
Why would she hit it at Chae Yeon
when Min Kyoung was there?

611
00:29:07,584 --> 00:29:09,351
(The coach is frustrated
that things aren't going as planned.)

612
00:29:11,844 --> 00:29:13,122
It's another serve by Ui Jeong.

613
00:29:13,123 --> 00:29:14,724
(Ui Jeong's another serve)

614
00:29:19,695 --> 00:29:21,764
(Setting to the left?)

615
00:29:22,932 --> 00:29:24,066
(Seung Ju's strike)

616
00:29:24,867 --> 00:29:26,769
(Iron wall defense)

617
00:29:28,104 --> 00:29:30,239
(Setting to the left again?)

618
00:29:31,724 --> 00:29:33,176
Min Kyoung dives to save it!

619
00:29:36,591 --> 00:29:38,912
- Nice defense!
- That was an amazing defense!

620
00:29:38,937 --> 00:29:40,362
She jumps and strikes!

621
00:29:40,583 --> 00:29:40,983
(Whistle)

622
00:29:42,171 --> 00:29:43,171
That's a net violation.

623
00:29:43,172 --> 00:29:44,933
She touched the net!

624
00:29:49,058 --> 00:29:50,426
(A net violation by Altos)

625
00:29:50,465 --> 00:29:52,061
- It's a net violation
- It's a net touch.

626
00:29:54,591 --> 00:29:55,591
It's 2 to 2.

627
00:29:55,592 --> 00:29:57,433
(Third set, Altos 2 : Wonder Dogs 2)

628
00:29:58,167 --> 00:30:01,570
(Seung Ju's serve to keep the momentum)

629
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:06,232
Ui Jeong keeps it alive.

630
00:30:06,629 --> 00:30:07,629
Min Kyoung.

631
00:30:08,847 --> 00:30:10,436
The defender receives the attack.

632
00:30:11,013 --> 00:30:15,084
(Finally, the chance
to attack on the right!)

633
00:30:15,783 --> 00:30:17,977
A powerful strike by Young In!

634
00:30:19,622 --> 00:30:22,024
(The middle blocker follows her quickly.)

635
00:30:22,825 --> 00:30:26,529
(She fires the spike through the gap,
not a straight shot again.)

636
00:30:27,396 --> 00:30:29,698
(Frustrated)

637
00:30:30,423 --> 00:30:32,591
The opponents are ready to block! A spike!

638
00:30:33,136 --> 00:30:35,872
(Young In isn't getting ready
to attack again.)

639
00:30:36,204 --> 00:30:37,997
Young In, why aren't you getting ready
to go again?

640
00:30:39,775 --> 00:30:42,645
(The court is as fierce as a war zone.)

641
00:30:42,940 --> 00:30:43,940
To the middle.

642
00:30:44,480 --> 00:30:47,283
(The ball flies to the right again.)

643
00:30:47,472 --> 00:30:48,472
Pass it to her again.

644
00:30:50,359 --> 00:30:51,654
(Hesitating)

645
00:30:53,557 --> 00:30:55,159
(The ball is set to the left.)

646
00:30:55,184 --> 00:30:58,895
The push shot succeeds!

647
00:30:58,896 --> 00:31:01,954
- Guys, we're doing great now.
- Yes, we are.

648
00:31:02,741 --> 00:31:06,035
Young In! Get ready right away!
Can't you spike twice in a row?

649
00:31:06,036 --> 00:31:08,471
- I can.
- Just hit it! It's okay!

650
00:31:08,726 --> 00:31:11,040
- Give them a straight shot!
- Okay.

651
00:31:11,146 --> 00:31:13,432
Don't overthink. You're thinking too much.

652
00:31:15,578 --> 00:31:19,248
(Another serve by Seung Ju)

653
00:31:24,353 --> 00:31:26,094
- It's blocked!
- It's saved.

654
00:31:26,095 --> 00:31:27,123
(Unstable defense)

655
00:31:27,669 --> 00:31:30,635
- It's in! It's a score.
- Nice!

656
00:31:30,660 --> 00:31:32,128
(Another point with a push shot)

657
00:31:33,262 --> 00:31:36,532
(Third set, Altos 2 : Wonder Dogs 4)

658
00:31:39,035 --> 00:31:39,969
(Beckoning)

659
00:31:41,270 --> 00:31:44,076
(Dashing)

660
00:31:44,090 --> 00:31:48,605
Coach Kim replaces the setter
with Ha Kyung, which means...

661
00:31:48,812 --> 00:31:51,118
the game isn't going...

662
00:31:51,119 --> 00:31:52,738
- as Altos planned.
- Exactly.

663
00:31:56,619 --> 00:31:59,622
(Seung Ju's third serve in a row)

664
00:32:02,265 --> 00:32:03,265
Ha Kyung.

665
00:32:03,266 --> 00:32:05,595
(Nice setting by Ha Kyung)

666
00:32:06,429 --> 00:32:08,398
(Su Min's fierce strike)

667
00:32:09,491 --> 00:32:11,930
It's saved, handled calmly.

668
00:32:13,636 --> 00:32:14,894
The ball goes to the other side.

669
00:32:15,516 --> 00:32:16,516
Ha Kyung.

670
00:32:17,882 --> 00:32:18,882
A tip.

671
00:32:20,343 --> 00:32:21,678
(She defends it easily.)

672
00:32:22,255 --> 00:32:23,613
Young In!

673
00:32:23,614 --> 00:32:25,415
(It's another chance for Young In!)

674
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:30,887
Young In!

675
00:32:31,120 --> 00:32:34,156
(This time, she hits it straight!)

676
00:32:34,613 --> 00:32:35,613
A powerful strike!

677
00:32:35,614 --> 00:32:38,127
(It catches the defenders off guard,
just as planned!)

678
00:32:41,530 --> 00:32:43,766
(Another point for Wonder Dogs?)

679
00:32:43,767 --> 00:32:45,033
- A back-row violation!
- A back-row violation!

680
00:32:47,571 --> 00:32:48,571
No.

681
00:32:49,871 --> 00:32:51,424
Sorry.

682
00:32:52,208 --> 00:32:56,412
(Ha Kyung is
in the back-row Position One.)

683
00:32:57,213 --> 00:32:59,615
(A back-row player...)

684
00:33:00,149 --> 00:33:03,352
(attacking from the front row
is a violation.)

685
00:33:06,322 --> 00:33:08,758
(Frustrated)

686
00:33:08,767 --> 00:33:10,292
Yes!

687
00:33:10,359 --> 00:33:15,731
(Third set, Altos 2 : Wonder Dogs 5)

688
00:33:16,198 --> 00:33:19,268
(Seung Ju's fourth serve in a row)

689
00:33:22,316 --> 00:33:24,507
(Wonder Dogs get another chance
thanks to the strong serve.)

690
00:33:25,241 --> 00:33:27,677
(Setting to the right or the left?)

691
00:33:29,011 --> 00:33:31,101
(To the left!)

692
00:33:31,134 --> 00:33:32,378
Hit it!

693
00:33:41,501 --> 00:33:42,948
Hit it!

694
00:33:43,252 --> 00:33:46,762
Quick attack spike!

695
00:33:48,933 --> 00:33:52,116
If they keep up this momentum
from the start,

696
00:33:52,335 --> 00:33:55,382
they'll surely be able to surge ahead.

697
00:33:55,410 --> 00:33:56,872
Exactly.

698
00:33:58,492 --> 00:34:01,743
Chae-Rim! Nice!

699
00:34:04,380 --> 00:34:05,881
(Push it.)

700
00:34:06,582 --> 00:34:11,187
(Altos decides to stop the run.)

701
00:34:12,136 --> 00:34:15,124
The first timeout for Altos.

702
00:34:17,526 --> 00:34:21,196
(He stays silent, not saying a word.)

703
00:34:22,298 --> 00:34:26,335
(Reading the room)

704
00:34:27,603 --> 00:34:29,369
(Meanwhile, Wonder Dogs are
full of excitement.)

705
00:34:29,394 --> 00:34:30,271
Chae-Rim, well done.

706
00:34:31,051 --> 00:34:32,944
That strike was good.
You aimed it perfectly.

707
00:34:34,287 --> 00:34:35,287
We're doing great now.

708
00:34:35,288 --> 00:34:38,063
Su Bin, nice job. We're doing great.

709
00:34:38,637 --> 00:34:43,409
Do they have anything different
from what we expected?

710
00:34:43,591 --> 00:34:45,998
- No.
- No, right? We were right.

711
00:34:46,345 --> 00:34:49,145
How many times did Min Kyoung spike?
Only a few.

712
00:34:49,418 --> 00:34:52,577
When the rally is tough,
she often hits dinks.

713
00:34:52,750 --> 00:34:54,663
And we've got someone to focus on that.

714
00:34:54,737 --> 00:34:57,256
Someone to handle the dinks.
We must take care of that.

715
00:34:57,858 --> 00:34:59,668
They're just as we analyzed.
Once we get the ball,

716
00:34:59,669 --> 00:35:01,971
- pass it around, then score.
- Okay.

717
00:35:06,017 --> 00:35:07,524
Hey.

718
00:35:08,030 --> 00:35:10,429
Don't tip to the back from the left!

719
00:35:10,462 --> 00:35:12,342
- Not to the back!
- They're all in defense!

720
00:35:12,343 --> 00:35:15,317
They're all in defense!
Don't hit tips from the left!

721
00:35:15,318 --> 00:35:18,005
Since their Position Six is on the side,
the middle is open.

722
00:35:18,006 --> 00:35:20,634
- Okay.
- Go for the middle!

723
00:35:21,053 --> 00:35:23,893
You're giving them too many chances.
When they get one,

724
00:35:24,088 --> 00:35:26,335
- they attack everywhere.
- Okay.

725
00:35:26,555 --> 00:35:29,401
(Meanwhile, Wonder Dogs have no idea
about the opponent's strategy change.)

726
00:35:29,787 --> 00:35:33,707
(They stick to their plan
to block the dinks on the left.)

727
00:35:34,930 --> 00:35:38,066
Don't do dinks, especially from the left!

728
00:35:38,460 --> 00:35:43,272
Do they have anything special
other than what we discussed?

729
00:35:44,171 --> 00:35:47,783
(A tactical duel between a 30-year veteran
versus a first-year rookie)

730
00:35:49,004 --> 00:35:51,890
Although Altos won the first set,

731
00:35:52,037 --> 00:35:54,510
after that dramatic win in the second set,

732
00:35:54,511 --> 00:35:56,644
Wonder Dogs are now on a roll.

733
00:35:56,645 --> 00:35:59,728
(Seung Ju's serve)

734
00:35:59,729 --> 00:36:01,438
- Catch it!
- Let's catch it!

735
00:36:08,670 --> 00:36:09,670
Back C!

736
00:36:09,814 --> 00:36:11,097
Ha Kyung's back toss.

737
00:36:11,213 --> 00:36:12,775
(Left dink)

738
00:36:13,309 --> 00:36:16,479
(The middle is wide open.)

739
00:36:16,779 --> 00:36:19,382
(Things are going just
as the coach predicted.)

740
00:36:20,115 --> 00:36:22,851
(Will this attack succeed?)

741
00:36:26,512 --> 00:36:29,998
No one to get it!
They've got to defend those.

742
00:36:29,999 --> 00:36:32,668
Even though Wonder Dogs are leading
by a good margin,

743
00:36:32,962 --> 00:36:36,841
the tables can turn
with just a few small mistakes like that.

744
00:36:36,866 --> 00:36:38,606
The coach needs to improve on everything.

745
00:36:39,412 --> 00:36:40,412
The score is 6 to 3.

746
00:36:40,413 --> 00:36:42,971
(Chae Yeon's serve)

747
00:36:47,076 --> 00:36:49,045
(Hesitating)

748
00:36:49,600 --> 00:36:50,600
You should get it!

749
00:36:50,601 --> 00:36:53,548
(Her teammates dive to cover
Myoung-hwa's mistake.)

750
00:36:53,849 --> 00:36:55,926
(Defense fails.)

751
00:36:55,999 --> 00:36:57,598
Myoung-hwa! I told you
to move to the middle!

752
00:36:58,538 --> 00:37:01,056
- Sorry.
- I told you to move to the middle!

753
00:37:01,080 --> 00:37:02,013
Nice!

754
00:37:02,034 --> 00:37:04,925
- Okay!
- Nice one.

755
00:37:04,950 --> 00:37:07,118
(Altos are on a scoring streak.)

756
00:37:08,464 --> 00:37:11,466
- The momentum can shift at any moment,
- Of course.

757
00:37:11,467 --> 00:37:13,535
so they need to hold onto it
while they can.

758
00:37:14,470 --> 00:37:18,740
(Altos are riding the momentum.)

759
00:37:21,210 --> 00:37:22,110
Off the block!

760
00:37:22,111 --> 00:37:23,445
(Wonder Dogs lost a point off the block.)

761
00:37:23,446 --> 00:37:24,780
It's seven to five. Just a two-point gap.

762
00:37:27,350 --> 00:37:28,383
(Service ace by Altos)

763
00:37:28,651 --> 00:37:30,418
It lands inside the court.

764
00:37:30,419 --> 00:37:31,586
It's seven to six now.

765
00:37:32,555 --> 00:37:34,222
Chae-Rim, what did I tell you
about her serve?

766
00:37:34,223 --> 00:37:35,657
It's pushed forward!

767
00:37:39,295 --> 00:37:40,895
- Block it!
- We're okay. Go!

768
00:37:40,896 --> 00:37:42,997
(Barely pushed it over with a shaky play)

769
00:37:49,672 --> 00:37:51,106
A slide attack, and she scores!

770
00:37:51,907 --> 00:37:53,198
It's tied at seven.

771
00:37:53,809 --> 00:37:54,967
Come on!

772
00:37:55,244 --> 00:37:56,077
Step up!

773
00:37:56,345 --> 00:37:58,546
- They still need to keep pushing.
- Young In.

774
00:37:58,547 --> 00:38:00,648
Yeah, they can't lose focus.

775
00:38:01,217 --> 00:38:02,017
Block it!

776
00:38:03,119 --> 00:38:04,052
Spike!

777
00:38:05,254 --> 00:38:06,187
Stay right there!

778
00:38:06,188 --> 00:38:08,757
(Wonder Dogs drop another point.)

779
00:38:09,525 --> 00:38:10,358
Sorry.

780
00:38:10,493 --> 00:38:12,527
Altos take the lead.

781
00:38:12,528 --> 00:38:13,928
(Third set, Altos 9 : Wonder Dogs 8)

782
00:38:14,497 --> 00:38:17,733
(Captain Min Kyoung's serve)

783
00:38:22,505 --> 00:38:23,738
No, no!

784
00:38:23,739 --> 00:38:27,508
(Another passing error)

785
00:38:27,843 --> 00:38:29,443
The Altos lead 10 to 8, up by 2.

786
00:38:29,445 --> 00:38:30,880
(Third set, Altos 10 : Wonder Dogs 8)

787
00:38:30,880 --> 00:38:34,616
We need to take full control
while we have the momentum.

788
00:38:34,617 --> 00:38:39,454
They've sent in Ha Kyung as the setter,
and she's more experienced.

789
00:38:39,822 --> 00:38:41,756
Their play is getting stronger now.

790
00:38:42,167 --> 00:38:44,468
Just as expected from Coach Ho Chul.
Brilliant move.

791
00:38:44,493 --> 00:38:46,127
(Altos have shifted the momentum.)

792
00:38:46,862 --> 00:38:48,396
(Let's go for it!)

793
00:38:52,418 --> 00:38:56,270
Pilseung Wonder Dogs call
for their first timeout.

794
00:38:57,039 --> 00:38:58,630
- Are we running zero now?
- Yes.

795
00:38:59,108 --> 00:39:00,875
- We're locked in rotation now, so...
- Na-Yeon.

796
00:39:00,876 --> 00:39:01,642
Yes?

797
00:39:02,678 --> 00:39:03,678
What play did you call?

798
00:39:03,679 --> 00:39:05,246
That we should go with back A and...

799
00:39:05,247 --> 00:39:06,747
You've got Young In.

800
00:39:07,149 --> 00:39:08,783
Why not use her for a back attack?

801
00:39:09,018 --> 00:39:09,884
- Use her.
- Okay.

802
00:39:10,619 --> 00:39:14,956
Young In isn't on her A-game either,
and she's not getting attacking chances.

803
00:39:16,192 --> 00:39:17,559
Give Young In some chances.

804
00:39:17,560 --> 00:39:19,795
Use her. Give her more sets.

805
00:39:19,795 --> 00:39:20,628
She'll do great.

806
00:39:20,629 --> 00:39:22,530
(Trust me on this.)

807
00:39:23,065 --> 00:39:25,233
When we're up
against a rookie team like them,

808
00:39:25,611 --> 00:39:28,012
they usually don't have
strong blocking skills.

809
00:39:28,037 --> 00:39:30,005
So don't try to make it complicated.

810
00:39:30,339 --> 00:39:33,408
If worst comes to worst,
just smash it into the block.

811
00:39:33,409 --> 00:39:34,509
Don't try to set it too far.

812
00:39:34,510 --> 00:39:36,745
- Let's cover for each other.
- Okay.

813
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:38,680
- Okay!
- Let's go!

814
00:39:38,814 --> 00:39:40,381
- One, two, three. Let's go!
- Let's go!

815
00:39:40,382 --> 00:39:41,148
Let's go!

816
00:39:41,684 --> 00:39:43,485
(Just set it to Young In.)

817
00:39:43,886 --> 00:39:46,054
(Just smash it into the block.)

818
00:39:46,589 --> 00:39:49,057
(The coaches'
tactical showdown is back on.)

819
00:39:49,692 --> 00:39:51,593
(Min Kyoung's serve)

820
00:39:53,696 --> 00:39:54,796
Back-row pass.

821
00:39:55,998 --> 00:39:58,500
(Setting to Young In as planned.)

822
00:40:02,872 --> 00:40:04,806
A powerful spike from the right back!
Great move!

823
00:40:06,742 --> 00:40:08,676
(The play worked!)

824
00:40:09,044 --> 00:40:09,910
Thanks.

825
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:12,647
(The rookie coach is one step ahead.)

826
00:40:12,648 --> 00:40:15,350
Na-Yeon! That was too high.

827
00:40:15,384 --> 00:40:16,584
Too high. Make it quicker.

828
00:40:16,585 --> 00:40:17,585
(Got it.)

829
00:40:18,053 --> 00:40:19,387
Try not to push it back too far.

830
00:40:19,388 --> 00:40:20,488
(Well, well...)

831
00:40:21,323 --> 00:40:22,657
(Third set, Altos 12 : Wonder Dogs 10)

832
00:40:22,658 --> 00:40:23,591
Serve!

833
00:40:26,262 --> 00:40:26,995
I got it!

834
00:40:27,196 --> 00:40:28,062
Stay where you are!

835
00:40:28,130 --> 00:40:29,664
Back her up! Cover her!

836
00:40:30,065 --> 00:40:31,098
Open attack!

837
00:40:32,034 --> 00:40:33,101
(It's blocked!)

838
00:40:35,504 --> 00:40:37,205
(If worst comes to worst,)

839
00:40:37,206 --> 00:40:38,907
(just smash it...)

840
00:40:40,376 --> 00:40:42,344
(into the block.)

841
00:40:43,245 --> 00:40:45,613
(The ball goes
right through the blockers.)

842
00:40:46,649 --> 00:40:47,649
Nice!

843
00:40:47,650 --> 00:40:49,551
(A brilliant play by the 30-year veteran)

844
00:40:49,551 --> 00:40:50,384
Nice play!

845
00:40:51,821 --> 00:40:53,088
Sorry, my bad.

846
00:40:53,556 --> 00:40:56,024
Myoung Hwa, close the block.

847
00:40:57,293 --> 00:40:59,594
(This is how it's done.)

848
00:41:00,062 --> 00:41:01,329
The score's 13 to 11.

849
00:41:01,330 --> 00:41:02,764
(Third set, Altos 13 : Wonder Dogs 11)

850
00:41:03,399 --> 00:41:05,200
(Na-Yeon's serve)

851
00:41:06,435 --> 00:41:07,268
My ball!

852
00:41:07,269 --> 00:41:08,469
(The ball...)

853
00:41:08,470 --> 00:41:09,737
(is up in the air!)

854
00:41:09,738 --> 00:41:11,005
Direct point!

855
00:41:12,942 --> 00:41:14,075
I can't believe they saved it.

856
00:41:14,076 --> 00:41:14,876
Hit it!

857
00:41:15,511 --> 00:41:16,144
Hit it!

858
00:41:16,145 --> 00:41:18,146
(She hits it...)

859
00:41:18,147 --> 00:41:19,447
(straight into the block.)

860
00:41:22,284 --> 00:41:23,985
(The ball hits her right on the head.)

861
00:41:25,521 --> 00:41:27,355
(Ouch)

862
00:41:27,923 --> 00:41:28,890
I told you. Close the block.

863
00:41:30,759 --> 00:41:32,326
- That's why it hit your head.
- Okay.

864
00:41:33,362 --> 00:41:36,130
(You got aced because you're a rookie.)

865
00:41:36,432 --> 00:41:37,532
It's 14 to 11.

866
00:41:38,267 --> 00:41:39,834
(Ui Jeong's serve)

867
00:41:40,202 --> 00:41:43,938
- I got it!
- Nice pass!

868
00:41:43,939 --> 00:41:44,705
It's up!

869
00:41:44,707 --> 00:41:45,941
(It's our time to strike back.)

870
00:41:46,508 --> 00:41:48,442
(Come on, Young In!)

871
00:41:48,444 --> 00:41:50,078
(Spike it!)

872
00:41:50,746 --> 00:41:51,679
It's a bit low.

873
00:41:51,680 --> 00:41:53,014
(The pass looks too low.)

874
00:41:53,015 --> 00:41:53,815
It's too low!

875
00:41:55,351 --> 00:41:57,519
(A scrappy series of hits)

876
00:41:58,053 --> 00:41:59,553
(Which means a free ball for Altos.)

877
00:41:59,788 --> 00:42:00,621
Back set.

878
00:42:00,622 --> 00:42:01,689
(Another spike into the block)

879
00:42:03,125 --> 00:42:04,158
(Smash it!)

880
00:42:04,159 --> 00:42:05,760
Point off the block.

881
00:42:06,795 --> 00:42:10,064
(Getting frustrated)

882
00:42:11,867 --> 00:42:13,768
(As expected,
the veteran coach is no pushover.)

883
00:42:15,170 --> 00:42:16,871
After Ha Kyoung came onto the court,

884
00:42:16,872 --> 00:42:19,774
Altos' attacks are looking
much smoother now.

885
00:42:19,775 --> 00:42:21,843
Yes, their set plays are working too.

886
00:42:21,844 --> 00:42:24,679
Young In seems off her game today.

887
00:42:24,680 --> 00:42:28,616
Na-Yeon sets it to the opposite hitter,
to the right side,

888
00:42:28,617 --> 00:42:30,918
and it seems a bit shaky today,

889
00:42:31,087 --> 00:42:32,319
and they're not quite in sync.

890
00:42:32,321 --> 00:42:35,723
So we're not getting many scoring chances
from the right side.

891
00:42:37,559 --> 00:42:39,593
It's the second technical timeout
of the third set.

892
00:42:40,829 --> 00:42:42,696
(A technical timeout is
automatically given...)

893
00:42:42,698 --> 00:42:44,666
(when a team reaches 8 or 16 points.)

894
00:42:48,837 --> 00:42:54,308
(Unlike other times,
the bench area is filled with silence.)

895
00:42:56,612 --> 00:43:00,648
Coach Yeon Koung hasn't said
a single word.

896
00:43:00,649 --> 00:43:02,783
She seems deep in thought.

897
00:43:04,011 --> 00:43:07,747
I've really been racking my brain.

898
00:43:08,649 --> 00:43:14,321
We've already tried various strategies
since the beginning.

899
00:43:17,024 --> 00:43:18,691
Na-Yeon, you're up.

900
00:43:19,026 --> 00:43:23,463
(She's made multiple substitutions...)

901
00:43:24,498 --> 00:43:29,969
(and various tactics
tailored for this match,)

902
00:43:31,472 --> 00:43:34,874
(but Altos have been scoring
relentlessly.)

903
00:43:38,479 --> 00:43:41,182
(Wonder Dogs can't afford to lose
their composure now.)

904
00:43:41,183 --> 00:43:44,918
In the end, we have to show everyone
what we've prepared.

905
00:43:44,918 --> 00:43:46,719
What we set out to do.

906
00:43:49,757 --> 00:43:50,824
Should we stick with this?

907
00:43:51,325 --> 00:43:53,593
- You want to sub in Jin?
- Yes.

908
00:43:53,594 --> 00:43:55,463
I think it's the right call.

909
00:43:55,463 --> 00:43:57,329
We can't turn it around like this.

910
00:43:57,331 --> 00:43:58,331
Okay, let's do it.

911
00:43:58,332 --> 00:43:59,431
I'll let them know.

912
00:44:01,202 --> 00:44:03,003
- One, two, three! Let's go!
- Let's go!

913
00:44:03,003 --> 00:44:04,170
- Let's go!
- You're up.

914
00:44:04,171 --> 00:44:05,138
- Now?
- Yes.

915
00:44:05,573 --> 00:44:06,973
Set your position first, toss,
then fall back.

916
00:44:06,974 --> 00:44:08,908
- Okay.
- Toss, then fall back.

917
00:44:08,909 --> 00:44:12,311
(Jin's father)

918
00:44:13,380 --> 00:44:14,246
Let's go!

919
00:44:14,248 --> 00:44:16,282
(Jin subs in for Na-Yeon.)

920
00:44:16,717 --> 00:44:17,583
Go, Wonder Dogs!

921
00:44:17,885 --> 00:44:19,619
Toss, then fall back.

922
00:44:20,554 --> 00:44:21,821
They've switched setters.

923
00:44:21,822 --> 00:44:23,456
Jin's back on the court.

924
00:44:24,325 --> 00:44:27,127
- Target it to Min Kyoung.
- Got it.

925
00:44:28,462 --> 00:44:29,696
(Taking a deep breath)

926
00:44:30,130 --> 00:44:33,299
I was given one last chance
to make it right,

927
00:44:33,734 --> 00:44:36,235
so I knew I had to seize this chance.

928
00:44:37,304 --> 00:44:38,437
(Against her former teammates)

929
00:44:38,439 --> 00:44:39,539
Serve coming up!

930
00:44:42,042 --> 00:44:44,910
I needed to show them what I could do.

931
00:44:45,713 --> 00:44:47,714
- Target it to Min Kyoung.
- Got it.

932
00:44:47,715 --> 00:44:48,748
(Min Kyoung is the target.)

933
00:44:49,049 --> 00:44:51,617
(That's the right side.)

934
00:44:54,421 --> 00:44:57,757
(Third set, Altos 17 : Wonder Dogs 11)

935
00:44:57,758 --> 00:45:01,094
- Go, Altos!
- Toss it up!

936
00:45:01,095 --> 00:45:02,329
Toss it up!

937
00:45:02,630 --> 00:45:04,898
To the front!

938
00:45:10,026 --> 00:45:11,626
(Powerful spike by Young In)

939
00:45:12,996 --> 00:45:13,796
Toss it up!

940
00:45:15,098 --> 00:45:16,600
(The new tactic works!)

941
00:45:16,601 --> 00:45:17,800
- Keep it up!
- Let's go!

942
00:45:17,801 --> 00:45:19,101
Good job!

943
00:45:19,836 --> 00:45:22,237
(Nice pass!)

944
00:45:22,773 --> 00:45:25,174
At this point,
the setter needs to find a way...

945
00:45:25,175 --> 00:45:28,344
to set up plays that use Young In.

946
00:45:28,345 --> 00:45:29,178
That's right.

947
00:45:31,882 --> 00:45:33,783
(Silent but furious)

948
00:45:37,187 --> 00:45:38,487
(Walking over quietly)

949
00:45:40,490 --> 00:45:42,191
(So Young is back in the game.)

950
00:45:42,192 --> 00:45:45,196
Substitution for the Altos' No. 1,
Lee So-Young.

951
00:45:45,220 --> 00:45:46,954
(Ui Jeong out, So Young in)

952
00:45:47,154 --> 00:45:48,912
With Ui Jeong out and So Young in,

953
00:45:49,266 --> 00:45:50,966
the Altos' defense is
outstanding right now,

954
00:45:51,065 --> 00:45:53,278
including Min Kyoung,
Chae Won, and So Young.

955
00:45:53,994 --> 00:45:55,963
(Looking intently)

956
00:45:57,732 --> 00:45:59,467
(Signaling the serve position)

957
00:46:00,668 --> 00:46:03,137
(Targeted serve)

958
00:46:04,071 --> 00:46:07,575
(Third set, Altos 17 : Wonder Dogs 13)

959
00:46:10,108 --> 00:46:13,180
Seung Ju scores on the serve!

960
00:46:14,982 --> 00:46:17,651
(A perfect serve
that broke through the pro defenders)

961
00:46:25,092 --> 00:46:29,063
(Now, it's the Wonder Dogs
that regained momentum.)

962
00:46:29,099 --> 00:46:31,766
This is how they shift
the momentum of the game.

963
00:46:33,993 --> 00:46:35,102
It's 19 to 14.

964
00:46:35,103 --> 00:46:36,571
(Third set, Altos 19 : Wonder Dogs 14)

965
00:46:39,607 --> 00:46:40,875
(Aiming the right as planned)

966
00:46:43,747 --> 00:46:45,029
So Young saves the ball.

967
00:46:45,412 --> 00:46:46,346
(It's a piece of cake.)

968
00:46:46,874 --> 00:46:48,766
So Young is so good.

969
00:46:49,416 --> 00:46:50,751
(So Young's defense)

970
00:46:51,619 --> 00:46:52,954
(Min Kyoung's spike)

971
00:46:54,255 --> 00:46:55,692
(She blocked the ball,
but it popped up high.)

972
00:46:55,693 --> 00:46:57,072
There's no one! Turn around!

973
00:46:57,385 --> 00:46:58,818
There's no one! Turn around!

974
00:46:59,139 --> 00:47:01,458
The defender sets the ball,
and a powerful hit follows!

975
00:47:01,971 --> 00:47:03,304
(Chae-Rim's smash)

976
00:47:03,911 --> 00:47:05,866
- Success!
- Right.

977
00:47:07,868 --> 00:47:10,804
(The Altos' defense is
slowly showing gaps.)

978
00:47:10,957 --> 00:47:12,185
Turn around!

979
00:47:12,209 --> 00:47:14,412
(Frustration is boiling over.)

980
00:47:18,183 --> 00:47:21,789
Min Kyoung, move your legs!

981
00:47:21,790 --> 00:47:24,985
Just reaching out
with your hands won't work.

982
00:47:28,364 --> 00:47:29,784
When you target Min Kyoung,

983
00:47:29,943 --> 00:47:31,776
their defense will cover.

984
00:47:32,083 --> 00:47:33,344
Then, spike to this side.

985
00:47:33,928 --> 00:47:36,364
(The previous attack)

986
00:47:38,265 --> 00:47:40,701
(When she hit straight at Min Kyoung,)

987
00:47:42,536 --> 00:47:44,772
(the defenders covered.)

988
00:47:45,673 --> 00:47:48,209
(This time, aim between the players
instead of straight.)

989
00:47:48,851 --> 00:47:50,119
(Understood.)

990
00:47:50,845 --> 00:47:54,949
(Third set, Altos 20 : Wonder Dogs 15)

991
00:48:00,054 --> 00:48:01,489
(A back set is given...)

992
00:48:02,576 --> 00:48:04,191
- Smash!
- That's it.

993
00:48:05,459 --> 00:48:07,628
(Back-to-back success!)

994
00:48:09,136 --> 00:48:12,202
Great play, Young In!

995
00:48:13,047 --> 00:48:15,869
Jin, nice set!

996
00:48:17,018 --> 00:48:19,018
- This is the attack we expect from them.
- Exactly.

997
00:48:19,538 --> 00:48:22,337
The toss to the right was
strong and precise,

998
00:48:22,370 --> 00:48:26,300
and it created a perfect setup
for Young In to attack.

999
00:48:26,552 --> 00:48:30,434
They need to keep the opponents
bothered by Young In.

1000
00:48:32,312 --> 00:48:33,312
It's 20 to 16.

1001
00:48:33,313 --> 00:48:34,779
(Young In, riding the momentum, serves.)

1002
00:48:44,255 --> 00:48:46,057
(A feinted surprise pass)

1003
00:48:47,443 --> 00:48:48,660
Dang it.

1004
00:48:49,694 --> 00:48:50,795
(To the empty space in the middle)

1005
00:48:51,220 --> 00:48:53,556
(Precisely)

1006
00:48:54,193 --> 00:48:56,045
- Hit the middle.
- Yes.

1007
00:48:56,069 --> 00:48:58,229
The Altos earn another point here.

1008
00:49:00,830 --> 00:49:02,965
(Third set, Altos 22 : Wonder Dogs 17)

1009
00:49:03,641 --> 00:49:05,276
(Targeted serve)

1010
00:49:06,144 --> 00:49:07,144
(Accurately to Ui Jeong)

1011
00:49:07,145 --> 00:49:10,204
- Great!
- Set it!

1012
00:49:10,791 --> 00:49:12,733
(Ui Jeong, hit it!)

1013
00:49:12,758 --> 00:49:14,752
Open spike!

1014
00:49:15,253 --> 00:49:17,163
(Another point lost)

1015
00:49:17,164 --> 00:49:18,587
Nice coverage!

1016
00:49:20,058 --> 00:49:21,610
(Every point they catch up,
the Altos pull ahead by one.)

1017
00:49:21,663 --> 00:49:23,850
The attackers are on fire in Set Three.

1018
00:49:25,026 --> 00:49:27,366
With attacks working well from both sides,

1019
00:49:27,379 --> 00:49:31,102
the Altos are pulling ahead in Set Three.

1020
00:49:33,237 --> 00:49:35,206
(The score is...)

1021
00:49:36,362 --> 00:49:38,469
It's 24 to 18.

1022
00:49:38,702 --> 00:49:40,438
Set point for the Altos in Set Three.

1023
00:49:44,082 --> 00:49:48,486
(Ultimately, they face
a cliffhanger showdown once again.)

1024
00:49:51,989 --> 00:49:55,626
- Altos,
- Altos,

1025
00:49:56,194 --> 00:49:57,762
- let's go!
- let's go!

1026
00:49:59,030 --> 00:50:00,465
(Look.)

1027
00:50:04,202 --> 00:50:06,771
(Delivered)

1028
00:50:10,108 --> 00:50:11,950
(Ha Kyung's serve)

1029
00:50:11,988 --> 00:50:12,988
Serve!

1030
00:50:15,113 --> 00:50:16,281
(Seung Ju's reception)

1031
00:50:16,781 --> 00:50:18,316
(Jin's set)

1032
00:50:18,950 --> 00:50:20,652
(And Myoung-Hwa's rapid strike?)

1033
00:50:25,022 --> 00:50:26,924
(Seung Ju's slam!)

1034
00:50:31,746 --> 00:50:33,915
(Myoung-Hwa drew both blockers,)

1035
00:50:35,291 --> 00:50:38,161
(and Seung Ju scored in the open spot.)

1036
00:50:39,098 --> 00:50:41,906
Setter Jin is using
both left and right sides evenly,

1037
00:50:41,991 --> 00:50:43,510
boosting the attack success rate.

1038
00:50:46,544 --> 00:50:49,914
(Dumbfounded)

1039
00:50:52,743 --> 00:50:54,043
It's 24 to 19.

1040
00:50:54,422 --> 00:50:57,023
The Wonder Dogs even...

1041
00:50:57,095 --> 00:51:00,291
pulled off a dramatic comeback
at 20 to 24 in Set Two.

1042
00:51:00,742 --> 00:51:03,643
Exactly. Now, for the Wonder Dogs
to turn things around,

1043
00:51:03,801 --> 00:51:06,383
- they need some consecutive points.
- Right.

1044
00:51:06,516 --> 00:51:08,132
Let's go!

1045
00:51:08,133 --> 00:51:09,634
(Let's go for it!)

1046
00:51:10,442 --> 00:51:11,442
Let's do this.

1047
00:51:12,703 --> 00:51:14,471
(Jin's serve)

1048
00:51:16,847 --> 00:51:17,861
That's it! Go!

1049
00:51:18,860 --> 00:51:20,344
Ha Kyung to the opposite side.

1050
00:51:20,369 --> 00:51:21,669
(Left spike...)

1051
00:51:22,163 --> 00:51:23,163
Su Min's tip.

1052
00:51:23,164 --> 00:51:25,349
(A tip from the left?)

1053
00:51:26,053 --> 00:51:27,745
I told you not to do that!

1054
00:51:29,183 --> 00:51:30,183
Hey!

1055
00:51:31,216 --> 00:51:32,216
Seung Ju.

1056
00:51:33,124 --> 00:51:34,459
(Despite the block...)

1057
00:51:34,495 --> 00:51:36,168
The defense covers. A back set!

1058
00:51:38,008 --> 00:51:39,008
Young In.

1059
00:51:40,364 --> 00:51:41,565
(The ball is slightly mishit.)

1060
00:51:42,266 --> 00:51:43,700
(The next player of the Altos is...)

1061
00:51:43,701 --> 00:51:44,760
Ui Jeong's powerful hit!

1062
00:51:44,761 --> 00:51:48,305
(Ui Jeong's hit is out.)

1063
00:51:50,697 --> 00:51:53,497
The Wonder Dogs scored
two points in a row.

1064
00:51:54,824 --> 00:51:56,814
Just hit it!

1065
00:51:58,616 --> 00:52:01,379
Coach Kim Ho Chul must've started
to feel anxious now.

1066
00:52:02,820 --> 00:52:06,190
(The atmosphere on the court has
changed noticeably.)

1067
00:52:07,549 --> 00:52:09,651
(It's Jin's serve again.)

1068
00:52:11,896 --> 00:52:13,898
The reception faltered.

1069
00:52:14,893 --> 00:52:16,734
An underhand toss, and a spike!

1070
00:52:17,554 --> 00:52:19,504
- Good defense.
- The ball is saved.

1071
00:52:20,964 --> 00:52:21,964
Back set!

1072
00:52:22,357 --> 00:52:24,475
Hit it!

1073
00:52:26,154 --> 00:52:27,154
Young In!

1074
00:52:27,155 --> 00:52:28,821
Success!

1075
00:52:28,834 --> 00:52:31,249
The Wonder Dogs earn
three points in a row!

1076
00:52:34,919 --> 00:52:36,663
(This is it.)

1077
00:52:36,669 --> 00:52:37,989
Nice, Young In!

1078
00:52:39,743 --> 00:52:41,158
Young In, that was great.

1079
00:52:42,149 --> 00:52:44,542
It's a bit late,

1080
00:52:44,602 --> 00:52:45,644
but that's okay.

1081
00:52:45,668 --> 00:52:47,189
- Don't you remember Set Two?
- I do.

1082
00:52:47,213 --> 00:52:48,760
The comeback started right from there.

1083
00:52:50,526 --> 00:52:53,504
Now, it's time for Young In to shine.

1084
00:52:56,007 --> 00:52:58,343
(Jin's three consecutive serves)

1085
00:52:58,976 --> 00:53:00,778
(The target is...)

1086
00:53:01,345 --> 00:53:03,614
(Ui Jeong again.)

1087
00:53:11,188 --> 00:53:12,289
(Libero Chae Won's coverage)

1088
00:53:14,771 --> 00:53:15,771
Attack!

1089
00:53:16,794 --> 00:53:18,089
They made the save.

1090
00:53:19,360 --> 00:53:20,564
Myoung-Hwa blocked it.

1091
00:53:21,165 --> 00:53:22,933
(The ball crossed
into the opponent's court.)

1092
00:53:23,601 --> 00:53:26,838
(The next attack is C-pass.)

1093
00:53:29,006 --> 00:53:30,207
(Su Min's powerful hit)

1094
00:53:32,410 --> 00:53:35,513
(It went past her?)

1095
00:53:38,549 --> 00:53:41,212
- It's in.
- Yes.

1096
00:53:45,022 --> 00:53:48,459
(They were stopped
right at the brink of a comeback.)

1097
00:53:49,548 --> 00:53:51,835
With a score of 25 to 21,

1098
00:53:51,875 --> 00:53:54,098
the Altos took Set Three.

1099
00:53:54,099 --> 00:53:56,134
(The Altos won Set Three.)

1100
00:53:56,354 --> 00:54:00,226
What do you think
we're lacking compared to them?

1101
00:54:00,466 --> 00:54:01,586
Reception.

1102
00:54:02,379 --> 00:54:04,865
Reception? And? Are there too many?

1103
00:54:06,252 --> 00:54:10,047
We're not as lacking as you might think.

1104
00:54:10,771 --> 00:54:13,384
It's just with each small mistake,
such as a reception error,

1105
00:54:13,630 --> 00:54:16,997
a mis-toss, a timing error on the block,

1106
00:54:17,297 --> 00:54:20,004
points keep slipping away.

1107
00:54:20,417 --> 00:54:23,828
You're doing well,
so let's take it step by step, okay?

1108
00:54:25,836 --> 00:54:28,561
Young In, play confidently.
Why are you making that face?

1109
00:54:28,868 --> 00:54:30,895
How can your teammates trust you
on the court?

1110
00:54:31,708 --> 00:54:33,164
Do you want to sit out the game?

1111
00:54:33,968 --> 00:54:35,172
No.

1112
00:54:35,535 --> 00:54:37,122
We've got this.

1113
00:54:40,426 --> 00:54:42,426
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's go!

1114
00:54:43,273 --> 00:54:45,309
- Tell me if you want to sit out the game.
- No!

1115
00:54:46,045 --> 00:54:48,412
Get your head in the game.
How are you going to win like that?

1116
00:54:52,211 --> 00:54:53,791
Why is Young In so loose on the court?

1117
00:54:54,712 --> 00:54:57,621
She keeps acting pitiful.
Then, she shouldn't step onto the court.

1118
00:55:00,353 --> 00:55:02,126
I thought...

1119
00:55:02,900 --> 00:55:06,938
today's game was going tough
for our team...

1120
00:55:07,999 --> 00:55:11,291
since I wasn't scoring enough.

1121
00:55:12,171 --> 00:55:13,604
So I was feeling down.

1122
00:55:13,931 --> 00:55:16,741
Young In, have some strong determination!

1123
00:55:17,077 --> 00:55:20,544
Just hit it hard with confidence!
It's all right.

1124
00:55:21,956 --> 00:55:24,090
But I promised myself...

1125
00:55:24,091 --> 00:55:26,924
I'd never show my weak side
to the coach again.

1126
00:55:28,052 --> 00:55:31,195
Set four is a must-win
for the Wonder Dogs.

1127
00:55:31,196 --> 00:55:33,497
(If we lose this set,
there's no next chance.)

1128
00:55:33,962 --> 00:55:36,967
The fourth set begins
with a serve from Altos' Eun Seo.

1129
00:55:36,968 --> 00:55:38,736
(Eun Seo's serve)

1130
00:55:39,152 --> 00:55:40,231
The fourth set begins.

1131
00:55:43,836 --> 00:55:44,836
Jin.

1132
00:55:44,861 --> 00:55:45,830
(Jin's toss)

1133
00:55:46,530 --> 00:55:48,997
(Here's a chance!)

1134
00:55:50,447 --> 00:55:53,214
(A powerful spike)

1135
00:55:53,947 --> 00:55:54,947
A spike on the right!

1136
00:55:55,314 --> 00:55:57,080
(The ball is high in the air!)

1137
00:55:57,702 --> 00:56:00,535
(But there's no one to receive it?)

1138
00:56:04,635 --> 00:56:05,869
It hits the ground!

1139
00:56:06,735 --> 00:56:08,902
The Altos made an error.

1140
00:56:10,802 --> 00:56:13,535
(Yoon Young In scores!)

1141
00:56:13,535 --> 00:56:14,902
Let's go!

1142
00:56:16,602 --> 00:56:17,669
Nice one, Young In.

1143
00:56:17,669 --> 00:56:19,302
- Hit it confidently!
- Yes, Coach!

1144
00:56:19,769 --> 00:56:22,102
Looking at the overall atmosphere,

1145
00:56:22,402 --> 00:56:25,302
Yoon Young In must gain confidence
to strengthen the attacks.

1146
00:56:25,302 --> 00:56:26,369
Of course.

1147
00:56:27,269 --> 00:56:28,269
Pyo Seung Ju serves.

1148
00:56:28,269 --> 00:56:30,802
(Pyo Seung Ju will serve.)

1149
00:56:33,502 --> 00:56:34,902
She saved it well.

1150
00:56:39,002 --> 00:56:41,102
- A quick attack!
- That's a nice play.

1151
00:56:42,035 --> 00:56:44,802
(They shouldn't be underestimated.)

1152
00:56:46,669 --> 00:56:47,669
Sorry. My bad.

1153
00:56:51,569 --> 00:56:53,235
Jin!

1154
00:56:53,802 --> 00:56:56,235
(Do it with Young In.)

1155
00:56:56,802 --> 00:57:00,302
(They made eye contact.)

1156
00:57:01,702 --> 00:57:02,869
Kim Na Hee is the server.

1157
00:57:02,869 --> 00:57:04,035
(Kim Na Hee serves.)

1158
00:57:07,835 --> 00:57:09,369
(Wonder Dogs' chance to attack)

1159
00:57:10,169 --> 00:57:11,169
They saved it.

1160
00:57:13,869 --> 00:57:16,102
(The ball is tossed to Young In again!)

1161
00:57:16,635 --> 00:57:17,969
Young In!

1162
00:57:19,569 --> 00:57:21,435
(A powerful spike)

1163
00:57:23,002 --> 00:57:24,702
- Yoon Young In!
- That's it!

1164
00:57:24,702 --> 00:57:27,102
They should get a point here.

1165
00:57:27,702 --> 00:57:29,835
The players made a flawless attack.

1166
00:57:30,802 --> 00:57:32,169
Compared to the start of the match,

1167
00:57:32,169 --> 00:57:36,069
Setter Lee Jin
and Yoon Young In are gradually...

1168
00:57:36,069 --> 00:57:37,769
- getting more in sync.
- That's right.

1169
00:57:37,769 --> 00:57:38,802
(Altos 3 : Wonder Dogs 4)

1170
00:57:42,502 --> 00:57:43,835
Young In does great when Jin is in.

1171
00:57:43,902 --> 00:57:46,269
Her speed makes the hit harder.

1172
00:57:50,535 --> 00:57:51,635
Jin.

1173
00:57:52,002 --> 00:57:53,335
Go with Young In.

1174
00:57:57,869 --> 00:58:00,035
(Catching the great opportunity,)

1175
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:03,269
(Yoon Young In scores.)

1176
00:58:03,269 --> 00:58:05,535
Nice toss. Great job, Young In.

1177
00:58:05,935 --> 00:58:07,769
(Satisfied)

1178
00:58:08,235 --> 00:58:10,002
(The Wonder Dogs are on a roll.)

1179
00:58:10,702 --> 00:58:11,802
Take it easy!

1180
00:58:12,302 --> 00:58:13,469
Lee Jin tosses.

1181
00:58:14,202 --> 00:58:16,502
- Yoon Young In scores!
- Nice play!

1182
00:58:16,569 --> 00:58:19,569
(The strategy to use
Young In works perfectly.)

1183
00:58:21,369 --> 00:58:24,135
(They continue to climb.)

1184
00:58:24,869 --> 00:58:27,935
Let's do it again. Don't make errors.

1185
00:58:29,435 --> 00:58:31,835
(Fourth set, Altos 4 : Wonder Dogs 6)

1186
00:58:32,435 --> 00:58:34,569
(We must maintain this momentum.)

1187
00:58:37,702 --> 00:58:38,702
She tries a service attack.

1188
00:58:40,902 --> 00:58:42,569
She steps back and uses the tip!

1189
00:58:42,569 --> 00:58:43,869
(A sudden tip attack)

1190
00:58:47,369 --> 00:58:50,669
(A pro team's tough counterattack)

1191
00:58:53,902 --> 00:58:55,435
It's six to five. Just a point apart.

1192
00:58:55,435 --> 00:58:56,602
(Lee So Young serves.)

1193
00:58:58,635 --> 00:58:59,935
(The reception is unstable.)

1194
00:58:59,935 --> 00:59:00,935
It hits the net.

1195
00:59:02,002 --> 00:59:04,569
(Will the ball go to the opposing team?)

1196
00:59:08,069 --> 00:59:10,135
(Lee Jin hits the tip!)

1197
00:59:11,635 --> 00:59:12,635
It's the tip!

1198
00:59:12,635 --> 00:59:14,202
(Striking back with the same attack)

1199
00:59:14,535 --> 00:59:15,535
Good job.

1200
00:59:16,935 --> 00:59:18,669
- They did it too.
- They gave back what they got!

1201
00:59:18,669 --> 00:59:20,302
It's like replying
to a letter you receive.

1202
00:59:21,602 --> 00:59:22,669
(Not the reply he wanted)

1203
00:59:22,669 --> 00:59:23,969
This isn't a freeze frame.

1204
00:59:28,102 --> 00:59:30,635
The Wonder Dogs must keep their lead.

1205
00:59:31,535 --> 00:59:33,602
And the one we've been waiting for.

1206
00:59:34,069 --> 00:59:35,435
- Today's Myoung-Hwa.
- Yes.

1207
00:59:35,669 --> 00:59:36,935
Moon Myoung-Hwa serves.

1208
00:59:36,935 --> 00:59:38,002
(The Queen of Serves reappears.)

1209
00:59:38,835 --> 00:59:41,635
(In the second set alone,)

1210
00:59:43,369 --> 00:59:47,069
(the Queen of Serves scored
with two service aces.)

1211
00:59:47,969 --> 00:59:50,135
(Can she deliver a service ace
in the fourth set too?)

1212
00:59:50,369 --> 00:59:51,602
Myoung-Hwa!

1213
00:59:52,169 --> 00:59:54,102
(Yeon Koung points out a serve target.)

1214
00:59:54,502 --> 00:59:56,769
(Target area)

1215
00:59:56,835 --> 00:59:59,369
In 1, 2, 3. Nice serve!

1216
01:00:00,002 --> 01:00:01,002
Please!

1217
01:00:06,502 --> 01:00:08,369
(She shook up the defense!)

1218
01:00:17,702 --> 01:00:19,702
(Cheering)

1219
01:00:21,135 --> 01:00:23,569
(She hits a service ace again!)

1220
01:00:25,069 --> 01:00:26,402
Moon Myoung-Hwa!

1221
01:00:26,702 --> 01:00:27,869
I told you!

1222
01:00:28,835 --> 01:00:31,835
(The crowd erupts wildly.)

1223
01:00:32,635 --> 01:00:34,302
(We knew you could do it,
Queen of Serves.)

1224
01:00:34,635 --> 01:00:36,802
(It's her third service ace!)

1225
01:00:37,335 --> 01:00:40,302
(The mood quickly turns romantic.)

1226
01:00:40,935 --> 01:00:44,202
(It's a thriller on this side.)

1227
01:00:45,569 --> 01:00:48,602
It's the Altos' first timeout.

1228
01:00:49,302 --> 01:00:51,169
Whatever we say, she makes it happen.

1229
01:00:51,169 --> 01:00:52,769
Yes! That's today's Myoung-Hwa!

1230
01:00:53,702 --> 01:00:57,702
(Just thinking about it brings
a smile to his face.)

1231
01:00:57,735 --> 01:01:00,802
(Just thinking about it makes him angry.)

1232
01:01:02,435 --> 01:01:04,302
What are you doing?

1233
01:01:08,402 --> 01:01:09,869
You can't get the ball from the start.

1234
01:01:09,869 --> 01:01:11,335
The reception is not working.

1235
01:01:12,169 --> 01:01:15,069
Focus when you play!

1236
01:01:15,069 --> 01:01:16,302
Yes, Coach.

1237
01:01:16,302 --> 01:01:18,102
You're all doing great.

1238
01:01:18,469 --> 01:01:22,035
But focus on the basic things we need
to do.

1239
01:01:22,869 --> 01:01:24,302
In 1, 2, 3!

1240
01:01:24,302 --> 01:01:26,369
(Let's keep this momentum!)

1241
01:01:27,869 --> 01:01:29,202
(After the timeout, the Altos score.)

1242
01:01:29,702 --> 01:01:30,935
It's nine to six.

1243
01:01:30,935 --> 01:01:32,402
(Altos 6 : Wonder Dogs 9)

1244
01:01:33,335 --> 01:01:35,469
(Choi Jeong Min serves this time.)

1245
01:01:37,802 --> 01:01:39,469
(Unstable)

1246
01:01:39,469 --> 01:01:40,469
Pyo Seung Ju.

1247
01:01:40,902 --> 01:01:42,002
Lee Jin.

1248
01:01:43,202 --> 01:01:45,069
(The Altos block it.)

1249
01:01:45,969 --> 01:01:46,969
They saved the ball.

1250
01:01:49,835 --> 01:01:51,969
She should receive it
and make a free ball!

1251
01:01:55,502 --> 01:01:56,702
It hit the net.

1252
01:01:57,969 --> 01:02:00,469
(The Altos get another point
to close the gap.)

1253
01:02:00,635 --> 01:02:02,002
Seung Ju, what did I tell you
about the reception?

1254
01:02:02,269 --> 01:02:04,102
Move at the same time,
not wait for the ball!

1255
01:02:04,102 --> 01:02:05,102
Understood.

1256
01:02:06,302 --> 01:02:08,069
(After Seung Ju's reception error,)

1257
01:02:09,835 --> 01:02:10,835
Go Ui Jeong!

1258
01:02:10,835 --> 01:02:12,802
(the Wonder Dogs lose a point
by a touch out.)

1259
01:02:13,035 --> 01:02:15,902
(The Altos aggressively catch up.)

1260
01:02:16,069 --> 01:02:17,769
You've got this, Go Ui Jeong!

1261
01:02:17,769 --> 01:02:19,302
(Altos 8 : Wonder Dogs 10)

1262
01:02:19,802 --> 01:02:22,235
(Setter Park Eun Seo serves next.)

1263
01:02:22,235 --> 01:02:24,302
Park Eun Seo may be a setter,

1264
01:02:24,302 --> 01:02:26,769
- but she's quite good at serving.
- You're right.

1265
01:02:30,769 --> 01:02:32,802
(The reception is shaky again.)

1266
01:02:35,502 --> 01:02:37,002
(They fail to defend afterward.)

1267
01:02:37,002 --> 01:02:38,102
Park Eun Seo scores with a serve.

1268
01:02:39,802 --> 01:02:42,902
(Altos 10 : Wonder Dogs 12)

1269
01:02:43,302 --> 01:02:47,602
(The mood feels unusual.)

1270
01:02:48,402 --> 01:02:49,402
Sorry.

1271
01:02:50,035 --> 01:02:51,869
Pyo Seoung Ju is struggling.

1272
01:02:51,869 --> 01:02:53,569
(The captain is losing her composure.)

1273
01:02:54,635 --> 01:02:57,402
(We can't go on like this.)

1274
01:02:57,502 --> 01:02:58,502
Song Hee!

1275
01:02:58,669 --> 01:03:00,035
(Come here.)

1276
01:03:00,069 --> 01:03:01,069
Switch with Seung Ju.

1277
01:03:02,235 --> 01:03:03,235
Right now.

1278
01:03:05,469 --> 01:03:07,902
Pyo Seung Ju steps out,
and Han Song Hee is in.

1279
01:03:09,035 --> 01:03:12,269
If the Wonder Dogs lose this,

1280
01:03:12,269 --> 01:03:14,002
there will be no more sets.

1281
01:03:15,202 --> 01:03:17,035
(It was urgent enough...)

1282
01:03:17,335 --> 01:03:19,802
(to replace the captain.)

1283
01:03:20,069 --> 01:03:22,202
(The game continues.)

1284
01:03:30,002 --> 01:03:31,002
Spike!

1285
01:03:31,002 --> 01:03:32,535
(They fail to defend again.)

1286
01:03:32,535 --> 01:03:33,535
Jeon Su Min.

1287
01:03:33,535 --> 01:03:35,569
(Altos 11 : Wonder Dogs 12)

1288
01:03:35,869 --> 01:03:36,869
My mistake.

1289
01:03:37,902 --> 01:03:38,902
A mistake?

1290
01:03:39,235 --> 01:03:40,302
What a nonsense.

1291
01:03:42,069 --> 01:03:44,835
(The Altos are closing in relentlessly.)

1292
01:03:45,535 --> 01:03:48,502
(It's a tense battle for a point.)

1293
01:03:48,769 --> 01:03:51,002
(What kind of strategy
should they think of...)

1294
01:03:54,102 --> 01:03:56,569
(to win the fourth set?)

1295
01:03:58,569 --> 01:04:01,235
We'll have to disband if we lose.

1296
01:04:01,369 --> 01:04:05,169
So I just decided to focus on the game.

1297
01:04:05,202 --> 01:04:10,169
(Focus on the game first.)

1298
01:04:14,569 --> 01:04:16,035
(A short reception)

1299
01:04:16,069 --> 01:04:17,269
(Dashing)

1300
01:04:18,602 --> 01:04:21,602
(Lee Jin covers quickly.)

1301
01:04:21,902 --> 01:04:23,235
They put it over the net fast.

1302
01:04:26,369 --> 01:04:27,369
Spike!

1303
01:04:29,435 --> 01:04:31,002
(Lee Jin's dig)

1304
01:04:31,035 --> 01:04:32,169
The ball shoots up.

1305
01:04:33,302 --> 01:04:34,302
Kim Na Hee!

1306
01:04:36,835 --> 01:04:37,835
A rebound hit!

1307
01:04:38,402 --> 01:04:39,402
Calmly.

1308
01:04:43,369 --> 01:04:45,035
She tipped it over the net.

1309
01:04:46,802 --> 01:04:48,102
They saved it with a dive.

1310
01:04:48,869 --> 01:04:49,869
To Lee So Young.

1311
01:04:51,435 --> 01:04:52,435
Spike!

1312
01:04:52,435 --> 01:04:53,969
(The ball hit the hands.)

1313
01:04:54,235 --> 01:04:56,402
(Will it be a touch out?)

1314
01:04:58,702 --> 01:05:00,969
(Lee Jin saved again!)

1315
01:05:02,069 --> 01:05:03,202
It's tossed to Kim Na Hee.

1316
01:05:03,502 --> 01:05:06,235
Spike!

1317
01:05:11,602 --> 01:05:12,902
Send it higher!

1318
01:05:13,435 --> 01:05:14,569
Send it higher!

1319
01:05:15,935 --> 01:05:16,935
She defended it!

1320
01:05:16,935 --> 01:05:18,902
(Setting up by lifting a ball high)

1321
01:05:25,669 --> 01:05:28,902
(Did they save it?)

1322
01:05:30,402 --> 01:05:32,869
(Out)

1323
01:05:33,235 --> 01:05:34,402
Nice!

1324
01:05:34,402 --> 01:05:35,569
They made it.

1325
01:05:36,269 --> 01:05:39,835
- It's so hard to get a point.
- I agree.

1326
01:05:40,602 --> 01:05:43,302
They miraculously saved the ball.

1327
01:05:44,469 --> 01:05:45,635
(With Lee Jin's super dig,)

1328
01:05:46,263 --> 01:05:48,730
You have to cover those attacks like this.

1329
01:05:49,196 --> 01:05:50,796
Jin, nice!

1330
01:05:53,030 --> 01:05:54,330
It was this way!

1331
01:05:55,463 --> 01:05:57,763
(Exasperated)

1332
01:05:58,196 --> 01:06:01,863
(Fourth set, Altos 11 : Wonder Dogs 13)

1333
01:06:02,314 --> 01:06:04,227
(The match continues.)

1334
01:06:05,296 --> 01:06:06,430
They saved it. To the other side.

1335
01:06:07,463 --> 01:06:08,430
Su Min.

1336
01:06:09,863 --> 01:06:10,963
Jin's dig.

1337
01:06:11,330 --> 01:06:12,430
Nice, Jin!

1338
01:06:14,096 --> 01:06:15,696
She saves it and connects it
with a back toss!

1339
01:06:17,030 --> 01:06:18,130
A spike!

1340
01:06:18,130 --> 01:06:20,530
A powerful spike, and it's a point!

1341
01:06:20,996 --> 01:06:24,963
Setter Jin has been on fire this set!

1342
01:06:24,963 --> 01:06:26,296
Just hit it!

1343
01:06:26,296 --> 01:06:27,630
(Frustrated)

1344
01:06:29,663 --> 01:06:33,363
A tight match continues,
as they exchange blows.

1345
01:06:33,363 --> 01:06:36,296
(The score is back
to a one-point margin now.)

1346
01:06:41,496 --> 01:06:42,463
A powerful serve.

1347
01:06:43,396 --> 01:06:44,396
She handles it well.

1348
01:06:44,396 --> 01:06:45,796
(Young In's spike)

1349
01:06:45,796 --> 01:06:47,130
It strikes the right back row!

1350
01:06:51,363 --> 01:06:52,896
(A successful dig)

1351
01:06:52,896 --> 01:06:54,263
Don't give up!

1352
01:06:54,763 --> 01:06:55,963
The ball...

1353
01:06:55,963 --> 01:06:58,163
If we lose, we have to be disbanded.

1354
01:06:59,363 --> 01:07:00,196
She saves it!

1355
01:07:00,196 --> 01:07:01,296
She miraculously saved it!

1356
01:07:03,463 --> 01:07:05,563
(The Wonder Dogs gain another chance.)

1357
01:07:10,630 --> 01:07:11,663
Back attack!

1358
01:07:14,863 --> 01:07:15,863
So Young again!

1359
01:07:15,863 --> 01:07:18,630
(We can do this all day!)

1360
01:07:22,496 --> 01:07:24,263
(A smart tip by Eun Seo)

1361
01:07:24,263 --> 01:07:25,696
(No way.)

1362
01:07:26,096 --> 01:07:27,630
Nice defense!

1363
01:07:29,198 --> 01:07:31,127
(The endless brutal volley continues.)

1364
01:07:35,630 --> 01:07:36,863
Young In makes the set.

1365
01:07:37,630 --> 01:07:38,696
Underhand toss.

1366
01:07:39,938 --> 01:07:41,338
A spike!

1367
01:07:41,363 --> 01:07:43,030
She keeps it alive.

1368
01:07:45,230 --> 01:07:46,596
So Young spikes it back.

1369
01:07:46,596 --> 01:07:47,963
(So Young's spike)

1370
01:07:49,596 --> 01:07:50,530
The ball!

1371
01:07:52,130 --> 01:07:56,830
(Missed the defense)

1372
01:07:56,830 --> 01:07:58,796
That was a solid strike, though.

1373
01:08:01,238 --> 01:08:06,204
(Fourth set, Altos 14 : Wonder Dogs 14)

1374
01:08:06,930 --> 01:08:09,996
The Wonder Dogs allow them
to make it a tie.

1375
01:08:11,796 --> 01:08:13,296
I wanted to do better.

1376
01:08:13,896 --> 01:08:15,196
I really wanted that, but...

1377
01:08:16,996 --> 01:08:20,763
(Despite the tenacity they've shown,)

1378
01:08:21,896 --> 01:08:27,096
(the Wonder Dogs fall behind,)

1379
01:08:27,963 --> 01:08:31,930
(and allowed the tables to turn.)

1380
01:08:33,363 --> 01:08:36,830
(Their stamina is dropping.)

1381
01:08:41,663 --> 01:08:44,430
(Here comes another rally.)

1382
01:08:46,963 --> 01:08:47,863
Jin.

1383
01:08:49,730 --> 01:08:50,796
Right-side attack!

1384
01:08:55,096 --> 01:08:56,430
Chae-Rim to the other side!

1385
01:08:58,996 --> 01:08:59,996
So Young.

1386
01:08:59,996 --> 01:09:01,963
(So Young's spike)

1387
01:09:03,463 --> 01:09:04,663
- She saves it!
- Nice dig.

1388
01:09:04,930 --> 01:09:06,196
You have to go!

1389
01:09:07,496 --> 01:09:09,430
(A two-hit combination...)

1390
01:09:09,430 --> 01:09:12,063
(not by the setter?)

1391
01:09:13,530 --> 01:09:16,530
(The setter takes the final shot.)

1392
01:09:19,096 --> 01:09:20,830
- Jin!
- Jin!

1393
01:09:21,863 --> 01:09:25,096
(A spike by setter Jin)

1394
01:09:25,663 --> 01:09:27,430
Is it out?

1395
01:09:27,863 --> 01:09:29,063
You have to keep going!

1396
01:09:29,063 --> 01:09:30,963
(The attack is...)

1397
01:09:33,696 --> 01:09:35,230
- It's in!
- It's in!

1398
01:09:36,363 --> 01:09:37,596
It's in!

1399
01:09:39,630 --> 01:09:44,263
We got it.

1400
01:09:44,263 --> 01:09:45,396
Great!

1401
01:09:46,696 --> 01:09:47,730
It's in!

1402
01:09:48,963 --> 01:09:53,096
It's rare for a setter
to score with a spike.

1403
01:09:54,330 --> 01:09:55,263
Jin!

1404
01:09:55,563 --> 01:09:57,196
Good spike.

1405
01:09:59,730 --> 01:10:01,096
That was bold.

1406
01:10:01,096 --> 01:10:02,530
The score is tied at 15 to 15.

1407
01:10:03,996 --> 01:10:06,030
Guys, we'll go for this.

1408
01:10:06,030 --> 01:10:08,963
Watch if it's short or long.

1409
01:10:11,763 --> 01:10:12,930
It's Myoung-Hwa's serve.

1410
01:10:12,930 --> 01:10:14,696
This is a chance at last!

1411
01:10:16,030 --> 01:10:17,130
We can count on her.

1412
01:10:21,063 --> 01:10:22,996
(Nervous)

1413
01:10:28,330 --> 01:10:30,730
(That's clearly out!)

1414
01:10:31,130 --> 01:10:32,130
It's in!

1415
01:10:33,196 --> 01:10:34,196
It's not?

1416
01:10:35,563 --> 01:10:38,796
(Serve error from their go-to player,
Myoung-Hwa)

1417
01:10:38,796 --> 01:10:40,996
A single error could cost them
not just momentum,

1418
01:10:40,996 --> 01:10:42,796
but the game.

1419
01:10:43,730 --> 01:10:46,230
(After their comeback,)

1420
01:10:47,796 --> 01:10:49,730
It drops right in the middle.

1421
01:10:50,263 --> 01:10:52,763
(The Altos widen the gap
by breaking through the block.)

1422
01:10:52,763 --> 01:10:54,496
It's another point by the Altos.

1423
01:10:54,496 --> 01:10:57,130
The Altos gradually take control
of the game.

1424
01:10:59,696 --> 01:11:03,730
(The Wonder Dogs lose another point
after being blocked.)

1425
01:11:05,563 --> 01:11:09,096
(The Altos are on a roll.)

1426
01:11:09,596 --> 01:11:11,163
The score is 21 to 17.

1427
01:11:11,163 --> 01:11:13,963
If they fail to catch up here,
it'll be harder.

1428
01:11:15,396 --> 01:11:17,096
We could attack from the right side too.

1429
01:11:17,930 --> 01:11:19,330
Trailing by four points.

1430
01:11:22,730 --> 01:11:23,930
The ball grazes the net.

1431
01:11:25,563 --> 01:11:28,363
(A back toss to the right side by Jin)

1432
01:11:28,830 --> 01:11:29,896
That's it!

1433
01:11:29,896 --> 01:11:30,730
Score!

1434
01:11:30,730 --> 01:11:33,530
- The block goes out.
- Nice.

1435
01:11:33,530 --> 01:11:35,763
I told you to get into position early!

1436
01:11:36,363 --> 01:11:39,696
(Right-side attack is successful!)

1437
01:11:39,937 --> 01:11:41,070
Jin, nice pass.

1438
01:11:41,696 --> 01:11:43,396
(Thanks to go-getter Jin,
the score is 21 to 18.)

1439
01:11:43,396 --> 01:11:44,496
It's 21 to 18.

1440
01:11:44,930 --> 01:11:48,063
It'd be great if they could close the gap
by one more point!

1441
01:11:50,663 --> 01:11:51,730
Jin!

1442
01:11:53,430 --> 01:11:55,463
Watch for a-pass.

1443
01:11:56,296 --> 01:11:58,930
Down by three, but they can close the gap!

1444
01:12:01,263 --> 01:12:04,230
Seung Ju has shown
many great serves today.

1445
01:12:07,430 --> 01:12:08,563
It grazes the net.

1446
01:12:10,863 --> 01:12:11,830
Quick attack.

1447
01:12:14,030 --> 01:12:15,430
She defends it well!

1448
01:12:15,430 --> 01:12:16,763
Go!

1449
01:12:18,396 --> 01:12:21,330
(Tenacious dig)

1450
01:12:24,963 --> 01:12:26,296
(A timing variation set!)

1451
01:12:26,296 --> 01:12:27,163
Timing variation!

1452
01:12:28,696 --> 01:12:30,696
(Screaming)

1453
01:12:31,896 --> 01:12:33,130
Sorry.

1454
01:12:36,063 --> 01:12:37,563
Down by four.

1455
01:12:37,563 --> 01:12:38,963
(It's okay.)

1456
01:12:38,963 --> 01:12:40,530
It's still within reach.

1457
01:12:47,096 --> 01:12:48,830
(Come on in.)

1458
01:12:49,930 --> 01:12:51,596
(The veteran coach's closing plan)

1459
01:12:51,596 --> 01:12:54,030
Altos substitutes Number Ten...

1460
01:12:54,030 --> 01:12:55,796
with Number 15.

1461
01:12:55,796 --> 01:12:57,496
Min Kyoung is in.

1462
01:12:58,263 --> 01:13:02,896
(The team's captain comes back in
with the support of her fans.)

1463
01:13:05,463 --> 01:13:07,996
Min Kyoung switches with Ui Jeong.

1464
01:13:13,363 --> 01:13:14,996
She looked so strong.

1465
01:13:15,630 --> 01:13:17,696
I was really overwhelmed.

1466
01:13:18,330 --> 01:13:19,996
The endgame moves show...

1467
01:13:19,996 --> 01:13:22,096
Coach Ho Chul's will to win.

1468
01:13:24,063 --> 01:13:26,030
Looks like he really came to win.

1469
01:13:27,230 --> 01:13:28,730
But we're going to take this victory.

1470
01:13:30,530 --> 01:13:32,330
Go for the middle and don't follow.

1471
01:13:32,330 --> 01:13:33,496
It's a floater serve.

1472
01:13:37,330 --> 01:13:39,796
(Captain Min Kyoung's serve)

1473
01:13:40,430 --> 01:13:41,830
My ball!

1474
01:13:41,830 --> 01:13:42,730
Jin!

1475
01:13:45,463 --> 01:13:46,930
(The block)

1476
01:13:46,930 --> 01:13:48,063
She saves it.

1477
01:13:48,063 --> 01:13:49,030
Jin.

1478
01:13:49,030 --> 01:13:50,163
Young In.

1479
01:13:50,163 --> 01:13:51,430
Na Hee makes the set.

1480
01:13:53,963 --> 01:13:55,130
Take it slow!

1481
01:13:55,130 --> 01:13:56,296
They're on their fourth try!

1482
01:13:59,063 --> 01:14:02,330
(It goes over the net!)

1483
01:14:02,496 --> 01:14:04,263
That's it.

1484
01:14:07,363 --> 01:14:08,296
Over the net!

1485
01:14:12,663 --> 01:14:15,930
(The Wonder Dogs' free ball)

1486
01:14:17,396 --> 01:14:18,330
(Piece of cake)

1487
01:14:18,530 --> 01:14:20,230
Min Kyoung's good save.

1488
01:14:24,930 --> 01:14:25,963
(One-touch!)

1489
01:14:25,963 --> 01:14:27,296
No! Don't give up!

1490
01:14:28,696 --> 01:14:30,863
(The Wonder Dogs need to pass it.)

1491
01:14:30,863 --> 01:14:32,196
But we're going to take this victory.

1492
01:14:34,196 --> 01:14:35,130
Su Min!

1493
01:14:38,463 --> 01:14:41,230
(A point by a block out)

1494
01:14:44,030 --> 01:14:48,496
- Two more points!
- Two more points!

1495
01:14:48,930 --> 01:14:51,696
(The substitution was a success.)

1496
01:14:52,096 --> 01:14:56,096
(The Altos are only two points
away from victory.)

1497
01:15:02,196 --> 01:15:05,363
After blocking five attacks
by the Wonder Dogs,

1498
01:15:05,363 --> 01:15:07,263
the Altos scored a point.

1499
01:15:08,030 --> 01:15:12,630
(Two more lost points mean their defeat.)

1500
01:15:13,763 --> 01:15:15,463
My bad.

1501
01:15:28,730 --> 01:15:30,830
(The rookie coach's lips are sealed.)

1502
01:15:30,830 --> 01:15:33,896
It got me thinking about so many things.

1503
01:15:33,896 --> 01:15:37,196
(The reeling players need...)

1504
01:15:37,196 --> 01:15:39,096
Things weren't going well.

1505
01:15:39,096 --> 01:15:40,163
(a new strategy.)

1506
01:15:42,730 --> 01:15:43,663
Jin!

1507
01:15:43,663 --> 01:15:47,663
It's okay. No need to panic.

1508
01:15:51,674 --> 01:15:54,007
It's okay.
You can send it to the back row.

1509
01:15:54,007 --> 01:15:56,274
Or set it to the front row.
That's fine too.

1510
01:15:56,607 --> 01:15:58,107
It's okay, guys.

1511
01:15:58,107 --> 01:15:59,474
(Coach trying to lift the team's spirits.)

1512
01:15:59,474 --> 01:16:03,674
It's crucial that the players maintain
their confidence.

1513
01:16:04,630 --> 01:16:06,597
(Min Kyoung serving again.)

1514
01:16:08,963 --> 01:16:10,663
(Jin's back set)

1515
01:16:12,897 --> 01:16:13,963
Altos' ball.

1516
01:16:13,963 --> 01:16:14,930
The Wonder Dogs spike.

1517
01:16:14,930 --> 01:16:16,730
But it's blocked.

1518
01:16:17,663 --> 01:16:19,863
(She can't lift her head.)

1519
01:16:23,230 --> 01:16:24,330
Let's go again.

1520
01:16:29,030 --> 01:16:31,263
(Holding back her words)

1521
01:16:31,930 --> 01:16:34,097
It's 24 to 18.

1522
01:16:34,097 --> 01:16:36,963
It's match point for the Altos.

1523
01:16:42,230 --> 01:16:46,030
(Divided by the net)

1524
01:16:48,797 --> 01:16:53,163
(The familiar cheering)

1525
01:16:55,930 --> 01:17:01,430
(But they're not cheering
for them anymore.)

1526
01:17:09,763 --> 01:17:12,363
(Su Bin, released from Altos in 2023)

1527
01:17:16,097 --> 01:17:18,430
(Jin, released from Altos in 2023)

1528
01:17:20,663 --> 01:17:23,330
(Hye In, released from Altos in 2025)

1529
01:17:40,463 --> 01:17:41,363
I'm so sorry.

1530
01:17:42,497 --> 01:17:43,663
No, it's okay.

1531
01:17:44,797 --> 01:17:48,430
(Fourth set, Altos 25 : Wonder Dogs 18)

1532
01:18:02,563 --> 01:18:05,648
The pros were on a whole different level.

1533
01:18:07,730 --> 01:18:11,463
Here are today's results.
The Altos win the fourth set, 25 to 18.

1534
01:18:11,463 --> 01:18:13,397
That makes the set score three to one.

1535
01:18:13,397 --> 01:18:15,530
It ends with an Altos victory.

1536
01:18:15,530 --> 01:18:16,763
- Good game.
- Good game.

1537
01:18:21,963 --> 01:18:24,930
It's the Wonder Dogs' first bitter defeat.

1538
01:18:26,830 --> 01:18:30,363
(Coach Yeon Kyoung is not used to losing.)

1539
01:18:30,363 --> 01:18:31,897
I didn't feel great.

1540
01:18:34,897 --> 01:18:38,597
(She's at a loss for words.)

1541
01:18:41,297 --> 01:18:42,563
I'm a bit upset too.

1542
01:18:45,463 --> 01:18:49,130
(They used the tactics they prepared.)

1543
01:18:51,430 --> 01:18:55,030
(And they worked.)

1544
01:18:55,697 --> 01:18:57,163
Remember, their blocking is weak.

1545
01:18:57,163 --> 01:19:01,063
(They fought hard on the court.)

1546
01:19:01,930 --> 01:19:03,463
(She smiled.)

1547
01:19:04,963 --> 01:19:08,663
(But were the pros still
too strong an opponent?)

1548
01:19:12,330 --> 01:19:15,097
We prepared so much for this game,

1549
01:19:15,563 --> 01:19:17,830
but we didn't really get to show it all.

1550
01:19:17,830 --> 01:19:20,163
So of course, it was frustrating.

1551
01:19:20,163 --> 01:19:23,597
If I were on that court,
I'd be able to lead...

1552
01:19:23,597 --> 01:19:26,697
and I'd try to turn things around.

1553
01:19:26,697 --> 01:19:29,330
But I was there as a coach,

1554
01:19:29,330 --> 01:19:31,330
so it was a bit hard for me.

1555
01:19:33,497 --> 01:19:35,197
This was way tougher than our other games.

1556
01:19:35,197 --> 01:19:36,463
Why was this so tough?

1557
01:19:37,030 --> 01:19:38,763
- Coach, this was so much tougher.
- What?

1558
01:19:38,763 --> 01:19:40,697
- This was so tough.
- Why?

1559
01:19:54,030 --> 01:19:57,230
(Feeling conflicted)

1560
01:19:57,730 --> 01:20:01,397
I wanted to do more for the players,

1561
01:20:01,863 --> 01:20:04,697
but I felt like I wasn't doing enough.

1562
01:20:05,163 --> 01:20:05,963
(Sighing)

1563
01:20:08,197 --> 01:20:10,797
(This coaching job is
no walk in the park.)

1564
01:20:11,030 --> 01:20:12,530
I just want to go home and lie down.

1565
01:20:16,163 --> 01:20:19,430
(The Altos players greet their fans.)

1566
01:20:45,497 --> 01:20:49,563
(Jin's father in the yellow shirt)

1567
01:20:52,830 --> 01:20:53,897
Can I have a towel?

1568
01:20:54,163 --> 01:20:55,097
Thank you.

1569
01:20:58,630 --> 01:21:02,363
(Jin pretends to wipe sweat
so her father won't see.)

1570
01:21:05,297 --> 01:21:07,497
(A defeat they want to hide)

1571
01:21:08,963 --> 01:21:10,763
(Sighing)

1572
01:21:11,763 --> 01:21:14,930
(The locker room is still filled
with resentment over the defeat.)

1573
01:21:15,997 --> 01:21:18,197
(Cracking her knuckles)

1574
01:21:19,830 --> 01:21:23,530
I wanted to show them
that I'm a better player now,

1575
01:21:23,530 --> 01:21:27,130
and I really wanted to win.

1576
01:21:27,763 --> 01:21:28,930
That's why I was so upset.

1577
01:21:30,197 --> 01:21:33,730
Hye In, you're crying. Why are you crying?

1578
01:21:34,530 --> 01:21:35,663
You've improved so much.

1579
01:21:35,663 --> 01:21:37,197
Thank you.

1580
01:21:37,197 --> 01:21:38,797
You've improved too, Jin.

1581
01:21:39,830 --> 01:21:42,763
- Keep going, okay?
- Yes, coach.

1582
01:21:44,030 --> 01:21:45,697
I have a soft spot for them.

1583
01:21:46,897 --> 01:21:49,130
Well, how should I put it?

1584
01:21:49,130 --> 01:21:50,697
I could've been kinder to them.

1585
01:21:50,697 --> 01:21:53,997
I could've done more to send them
to better places to play.

1586
01:21:53,997 --> 01:21:56,597
Those thoughts have always lingered
in my mind.

1587
01:21:56,597 --> 01:21:59,197
They're the players who tug at my heart.

1588
01:22:00,063 --> 01:22:02,563
(Sighing)

1589
01:22:03,430 --> 01:22:06,463
(Team Wonder Dogs will disband
if they lose four games.)

1590
01:22:08,397 --> 01:22:09,930
(And they lost one today.)

1591
01:22:11,030 --> 01:22:12,097
Did they take one off?

1592
01:22:14,363 --> 01:22:16,063
It's hitting me now.

1593
01:22:16,630 --> 01:22:19,430
If we lose again,

1594
01:22:19,430 --> 01:22:21,397
we'd be in trouble.

1595
01:22:21,397 --> 01:22:23,163
It felt very real.

1596
01:22:23,163 --> 01:22:25,897
That we might really have to disband.

1597
01:22:26,963 --> 01:22:27,897
(One win and one loss)

1598
01:22:27,897 --> 01:22:30,197
(Their winning rate is 50 percent.)

1599
01:22:30,463 --> 01:22:32,930
I'll reveal the next opponent.

1600
01:22:33,830 --> 01:22:35,663
(After their first loss,)

1601
01:22:36,363 --> 01:22:39,163
(here comes the next opponent.)

1602
01:22:49,779 --> 01:22:52,454
(Korea's longtime rival)

1603
01:22:52,476 --> 01:22:54,443
(However...)

1604
01:22:55,176 --> 01:22:58,276
(Korea ranks 40th in the world,)

1605
01:23:00,643 --> 01:23:03,456
(while Japan ranks 5th.)

1606
01:23:03,497 --> 01:23:05,897
(This team stands at the heart of it.)

1607
01:23:06,595 --> 01:23:10,395
(The current champions
of Japanese high school volleyball)

1608
01:23:10,619 --> 01:23:12,452
(Shujitsu High School)

1609
01:23:30,585 --> 01:23:35,219
(No chance for players...)

1610
01:23:35,219 --> 01:23:38,185
(who aren't good enough.)

1611
01:23:40,619 --> 01:23:43,285
(They have a ruthless competition system,)

1612
01:23:43,719 --> 01:23:46,252
(and these are the ones who survived.)

1613
01:23:49,485 --> 01:23:51,019
Shujitsu High School...

1614
01:23:51,019 --> 01:23:56,219
is the team with the strongest teamwork.

1615
01:23:59,419 --> 01:24:03,552
Our determination to chase the ball
to the very end...

1616
01:24:03,552 --> 01:24:08,252
sets us apart from every other team.

1617
01:24:08,719 --> 01:24:13,019
(Volleyball built on grit
and determination)

1618
01:24:14,752 --> 01:24:16,652
Compared to Japanese volleyball,

1619
01:24:16,652 --> 01:24:20,319
Korean teams have weaker defense.

1620
01:24:23,785 --> 01:24:27,352
(Shujitsu High School's score prediction)

1621
01:24:27,585 --> 01:24:28,852
Three to zero.

1622
01:24:29,319 --> 01:24:32,052
We'll win three to zero.

1623
01:24:40,219 --> 01:24:44,085
(The very person who built
Shujitsu High School's system)

1624
01:24:44,619 --> 01:24:47,019
(Coach Nishihata Miki)

1625
01:24:47,685 --> 01:24:54,785
Kim Yeon Koung has been on court
as the world's number one,

1626
01:24:54,785 --> 01:24:56,885
but coaching and playing are different.

1627
01:24:56,885 --> 01:24:59,885
Since I have much more experience
as a coach,

1628
01:24:59,885 --> 01:25:00,952
I think I'll be better.

1629
01:25:03,952 --> 01:25:10,385
Korean players used to have
confidence and pride,

1630
01:25:10,385 --> 01:25:13,885
but I think the current players have
completely lost that.

1631
01:25:14,763 --> 01:25:16,497
We will win all matches.

1632
01:25:19,995 --> 01:25:22,995
(The rookie coach Yeon Koung...)

1633
01:25:23,229 --> 01:25:26,495
(awaits her first international match
as a coach.)

1634
01:25:31,702 --> 01:25:34,602
(Game day)

1635
01:25:35,095 --> 01:25:36,929
(Japan)

1636
01:25:39,929 --> 01:25:42,295
(Takamatsu Airport, Japan)

1637
01:25:50,929 --> 01:25:52,695
I really felt...

1638
01:25:53,195 --> 01:25:56,395
that I was making my coaching debut...

1639
01:25:56,395 --> 01:25:58,395
in this match against Japan.

1640
01:25:59,208 --> 01:26:01,175
As always,

1641
01:26:01,175 --> 01:26:05,375
I get nervous before a game against Japan.

1642
01:26:06,242 --> 01:26:08,316
There's always a bit more pressure
in matches against Japan.

1643
01:26:08,557 --> 01:26:11,624
(The rookie coach's international debut)

1644
01:26:14,757 --> 01:26:17,324
(Into the heart of enemy territory!)

1645
01:26:30,824 --> 01:26:34,057
I knew how crucial it was...

1646
01:26:34,057 --> 01:26:36,524
to win the Korea-Japan match.

1647
01:26:46,135 --> 01:26:50,351
(Third match venue)

1648
01:26:51,947 --> 01:26:55,114
(Shujitsu High School)

1649
01:26:58,314 --> 01:27:05,214
(The third gym at Shujitsu High School)

1650
01:27:05,647 --> 01:27:08,514
(This ordinary high school gym is...)

1651
01:27:08,880 --> 01:27:11,947
(transforming to hold
a Korea-Japan match.)

1652
01:27:12,214 --> 01:27:17,247
(Not only local Japanese staff...)

1653
01:27:17,614 --> 01:27:20,780
(but also the Japanese broadcast team
was fully mobilized.)

1654
01:27:28,614 --> 01:27:30,247
(A Japanese announcer is also present.)

1655
01:27:30,247 --> 01:27:31,714
(Naoki, MC)

1656
01:27:32,547 --> 01:27:35,447
(Japanese referees are also present.)

1657
01:27:36,147 --> 01:27:38,747
Your passionate cheering is
the greatest attack.

1658
01:27:39,080 --> 01:27:42,380
Please cheer with all your might.

1659
01:27:42,589 --> 01:27:45,247
(Cheering, you say? Just as we hoped.)

1660
01:27:47,314 --> 01:27:50,714
(The Shujitsu High School cheering squad)

1661
01:27:50,714 --> 01:27:52,580
(In the corner next to them,)

1662
01:27:54,380 --> 01:27:56,314
(a modestly set-up Korean broadcast booth)

1663
01:27:56,314 --> 01:27:58,014
The scale of the supporters is
out of this world.

1664
01:27:58,898 --> 01:28:01,431
(Just as the gym is packed with cheering,)

1665
01:28:02,347 --> 01:28:06,180
(the away locker room is
filled in orange.)

1666
01:28:07,214 --> 01:28:09,780
(The Wonder Dogs with 1 win and 1 loss)

1667
01:28:09,780 --> 01:28:12,314
(This is the Korea-Japan match
they must win.)

1668
01:28:12,580 --> 01:28:15,114
For a moment, the fresh joy
of the first victory lingered,

1669
01:28:15,114 --> 01:28:17,047
but was followed
by the sting of the first defeat.

1670
01:28:17,047 --> 01:28:19,780
The Wonder Dogs had claimed
their first win,

1671
01:28:19,780 --> 01:28:23,647
yet suffered a painful loss
against a pro team, the Altos.

1672
01:28:24,147 --> 01:28:26,614
The third match is an international one.

1673
01:28:26,614 --> 01:28:28,680
Moreover, it's a Korea-Japan match.

1674
01:28:29,680 --> 01:28:32,680
That's right. The Wonder Dogs
have now come to Japan...

1675
01:28:32,680 --> 01:28:34,914
to play this international match.

1676
01:28:34,914 --> 01:28:36,514
In Korea-Japan matches,

1677
01:28:36,514 --> 01:28:41,080
Coach Kim remembers being very strong
against Japan as a player.

1678
01:28:43,358 --> 01:28:45,058
Today, the Wonder Dogs face
Shujitsu High School,

1679
01:28:45,083 --> 01:28:48,249
known as the strongest high school team
in Japan.

1680
01:28:48,691 --> 01:28:51,224
Winning last year's
national high school championship,

1681
01:28:51,658 --> 01:28:53,924
three Inter-High School Championships,

1682
01:28:53,924 --> 01:28:56,491
and five Spring High School Tournament
titles,

1683
01:28:56,491 --> 01:28:58,893
they're now considered
the strongest high school volleyball team.

1684
01:29:00,024 --> 01:29:01,058
They're entering now.

1685
01:29:03,524 --> 01:29:05,158
It feels like
the Spring High School Tournament.

1686
01:29:07,691 --> 01:29:11,091
(Shujitsu High School players appear
one after another.)

1687
01:29:11,691 --> 01:29:15,524
(Peeking)

1688
01:29:21,858 --> 01:29:25,324
(Let's give it our all and win!)

1689
01:29:27,991 --> 01:29:30,058
(Gathering all at once)

1690
01:29:36,158 --> 01:29:37,091
Great!

1691
01:29:37,091 --> 01:29:38,624
(Senba Kokoro, Libero)

1692
01:29:38,624 --> 01:29:39,624
Slow down!

1693
01:29:40,824 --> 01:29:43,258
(Led by ace Senba Kokoro,)

1694
01:29:43,258 --> 01:29:46,758
(everyone starts spiking.)

1695
01:29:47,058 --> 01:29:49,991
(Sharp and agile movements)

1696
01:29:50,658 --> 01:29:52,591
They're hitting really well.

1697
01:29:57,091 --> 01:29:58,024
Left!

1698
01:29:59,991 --> 01:30:02,191
(A powerful spike)

1699
01:30:02,291 --> 01:30:06,891
Shujitsu players are stronger
than expected.

1700
01:30:07,391 --> 01:30:11,424
Our players need to stay
even more focused.

1701
01:30:14,124 --> 01:30:15,024
Feint!

1702
01:30:15,024 --> 01:30:16,458
(Rushing in)

1703
01:30:17,024 --> 01:30:18,458
Great!

1704
01:30:19,258 --> 01:30:20,224
Good.

1705
01:30:22,258 --> 01:30:25,724
(Shujitsu's intimidating movements)

1706
01:30:25,886 --> 01:30:27,219
(The cheering squad takes action.)

1707
01:30:27,453 --> 01:30:29,219
- Let's go, Shujitsu!
- Let's go, Shujitsu!

1708
01:30:29,219 --> 01:30:32,519
- Push, Shujitsu!
- Push, Shujitsu!

1709
01:30:32,519 --> 01:30:36,053
- Fly, Shujitsu!
- Fly, Shujitsu!

1710
01:30:36,053 --> 01:30:39,586
- Run, Shujitsu!
- Run, Shujitsu!

1711
01:30:39,586 --> 01:30:43,486
- Fire it up, Shujitsu!
- Fire it up, Shujitsu!

1712
01:30:44,453 --> 01:30:48,286
Over a hundred supporters are here.

1713
01:30:48,286 --> 01:30:54,719
Of course, the passion
of Korean pro volleyball fans is amazing,

1714
01:30:54,719 --> 01:30:57,719
but Japan has
its own unique cheering culture.

1715
01:30:58,286 --> 01:30:59,919
Our Korean away supporters will...

1716
01:30:59,919 --> 01:31:04,119
have to overcome being outnumbered
in the cheer battle.

1717
01:31:04,119 --> 01:31:04,953
Right.

1718
01:31:06,019 --> 01:31:09,186
(At the rising roar of cheering,)

1719
01:31:09,186 --> 01:31:11,886
(responding with a piercing stare)

1720
01:31:12,219 --> 01:31:15,086
During pre-game practice,
the cheering was incredibly loud.

1721
01:31:15,086 --> 01:31:16,686
Honestly, it made me feel a bit deflated.

1722
01:31:16,686 --> 01:31:18,986
Volleyball is really a battle of momentum,

1723
01:31:18,986 --> 01:31:20,886
and if the other side's cheers are louder,

1724
01:31:20,886 --> 01:31:23,319
the atmosphere can swing in their favor.

1725
01:31:23,319 --> 01:31:24,686
(The cheering is completely one-sided.)

1726
01:31:26,568 --> 01:31:30,602
Players often talk
about the other team's supporters.

1727
01:31:30,602 --> 01:31:31,902
But those are all just excuses.

1728
01:31:31,902 --> 01:31:35,935
Whether the other team's supporters come
or not doesn't matter.

1729
01:31:35,935 --> 01:31:39,435
We'll just focus
on preparing thoroughly...

1730
01:31:40,168 --> 01:31:41,602
to secure victory.

1731
01:31:41,602 --> 01:31:43,535
(We'll beat them!)

1732
01:31:43,535 --> 01:31:47,502
Players, please face each other
to exchange greetings.

1733
01:31:47,502 --> 01:31:49,068
We focus on the basics...

1734
01:31:49,894 --> 01:31:53,960
and execute the fundamentals properly.

1735
01:31:54,835 --> 01:31:56,302
We will win all games.

1736
01:31:56,302 --> 01:32:00,368
We will win through solid fundamentals.

1737
01:32:02,135 --> 01:32:04,435
We will show true volleyball.

1738
01:32:05,710 --> 01:32:08,976
(The strongest high school volleyball team
in Japan)

1739
01:32:12,410 --> 01:32:14,443
(The Wonder Dogs standing on the edge)

1740
01:32:14,480 --> 01:32:16,802
Now, we have nowhere to retreat.

1741
01:32:17,335 --> 01:32:18,802
Losing this match would be embarrassing.

1742
01:32:20,010 --> 01:32:22,743
We know we absolutely have to win.

1743
01:32:23,577 --> 01:32:27,077
The showdown between the Wonder Dogs
and Shujitsu High School!

1744
01:32:27,102 --> 01:32:29,735
(The Korea-Japan match!)

1745
01:32:29,976 --> 01:32:32,209
Move your legs first!

1746
01:32:32,435 --> 01:32:34,068
Let's go!

1747
01:32:38,668 --> 01:32:42,402
I believe taking the initiative early is
extremely important.

1748
01:32:43,668 --> 01:32:45,735
(Either we finish it,)

1749
01:32:45,735 --> 01:32:48,035
(or we get finished.)

1750
01:32:48,602 --> 01:32:50,402
(Kato Uta's serve)

1751
01:32:50,402 --> 01:32:51,468
The first set begins!

1752
01:32:51,835 --> 01:32:55,035
Mine! Set!

1753
01:32:55,035 --> 01:32:57,402
- They're shaken.
- Young In!

1754
01:32:57,402 --> 01:32:58,502
Send it far!

1755
01:33:00,502 --> 01:33:01,468
Hit it!

1756
01:33:05,500 --> 01:33:07,067
(An unexpected hellish defense)

1757
01:33:08,000 --> 01:33:11,839
(They never miss the ball.)

1758
01:33:13,918 --> 01:33:16,085
(A powerful spike on another level)

1759
01:33:19,952 --> 01:33:21,585
I felt threatened.

1760
01:33:21,585 --> 01:33:22,918
This won't be easy.

1761
01:33:22,918 --> 01:33:25,718
I believe we must win with no excuse.

1762
01:33:25,718 --> 01:33:27,052
Where should you hit?

1763
01:33:27,518 --> 01:33:28,552
(The rookie head coach designs...)

1764
01:33:28,552 --> 01:33:31,518
(the strategy to break
through the opponents' defense.)

1765
01:33:31,885 --> 01:33:35,885
(Do not let them attack!)

1766
01:33:36,518 --> 01:33:37,518
Nice block!

1767
01:33:37,518 --> 01:33:41,718
(No more losses.)

1768
01:33:41,718 --> 01:33:42,752
Let's go!
